/* 横向卡 · 纯化一个重组蛋白（第二门课：蛋白质工程与合成生物学）
   不对应捷克书的任何一道题。出处是她自己的课堂笔记 pesbexplain/data/ch2.js，
   那里是四十四个从讲义幻灯片转写的节点。这张卡用到其中十七个：
   2-27 分泌与浓缩 · 2-29 层析基础与读图 · 2-30 树脂与开跑前四查 · 2-31 五种模式 ·
   2-32 离子交换 · 2-33 疏水 · 2-34 反相 · 2-35 亲和与标签 · 2-36 Ni-NTA ·
   2-37 Strep/FLAG/MBP/GST/HALO · 2-38 抗体、凝集素、链霉亲和素 · 2-39 自制树脂 ·
   2-40 SEC · 2-41 标签切除 · 2-42 捕获中度精修 · 2-43 SDS-PAGE · 2-44 浓度测定。
   笔记的 points ＝ 幻灯片上有的；beyondPoints ＝ 笔记自己标明「课上没讲」。
   本卡凡是用了 beyondPoints、或者用了通用知识的地方，都当场标了「课上没给」。
   页码位置用 <span class="pg"> 标的是讲次和幻灯片号，例如 L4 s.20。 */

window.CARDS.push({
id:'pe-pur', cross:1, w:0,
q:'纯化一个重组蛋白 —— 从澄清的裂解液到一管定量好的纯蛋白',
qcn:'第二门课 · 一个四步框架 ＋ 一条顺序 ＋ 三层绝不能混（结合 / 洗脱 / 移除）',
sub:'主干说完约 90 秒 · 这门课自己的口试上丢分最重的就是这一题：他问洗脱，答成了切除',

cram:[
 {g:'开口 · 两条骨架先摆出来', gn:'这张卡不是一张方法清单。它是<b>两条能把任何方法安放进去的骨架</b>，方法只是填进去的例子。'},
 {n:'01', t:'骨架一 · 四步',
  ez:'“Every mode of chromatography runs the same four steps. You equilibrate the resin. You bind the target. You wash the contaminants away. Then you elute the target. Only one thing differs between modes. It is which property of the protein is exploited. And that property decides one more thing. It decides what you must change. You change that to let the protein go.”',
  ezcn:'<b>每一种层析模式跑的都是同样四步：平衡树脂 → 结合目标 → 洗掉杂质 → 洗脱目标。</b><b>模式之间唯一的差别，是「利用蛋白的哪一个性质」</b>——<b>而那个性质同时决定了另一件事：你要改变什么才能让它松手。</b>',
  big:'<b>所有模式都是同样四步：平衡 → 结合 → 洗涤 → 洗脱。</b>模式之间只差「靠什么结合」',
  en:'“Every mode of chromatography runs the same four steps. You equilibrate the resin, bind the target, wash the contaminants away, then elute the target. What differs between modes is only which property of the protein is being exploited. That property decides what you have to change in order to let it go.”',
  note:'笔记原话就是这一句：<b>所有模式都遵循这个顺序</b>，区别只在「靠什么结合」。<span class="pg">L4 s.8–10</span><br>组分的标签也是通用的：<b>INJ</b> 上样 · <b>FT</b> 穿透液（没结合上的全部） · <b>W</b> 洗涤 · <b>E1–E7</b> 洗脱 · <b>C</b> 最后清洗。洗涤和洗脱各约 <b>10 个柱体积</b>。<br><b>承重词</b>：<b>流动相</b>＝流过柱子、带着组分走的缓冲液；<b>固定相</b>＝不动的固体，通常是多孔树脂、膜或凝胶。不交代这两个，「层析」这个词就是空的。',
  good:'顺手能给的一句：拿到一张跑坏的图，<b>先看 FT</b>。蛋白在 FT 里 ＝ 根本没结合上；FT 干净但洗脱很少 ＝ 结合上了但下不来。<b>两者原因完全不同</b>，所以这一个问题就把失败分成了两类。（笔记标 beyond the slides）'},
 {n:'02', t:'骨架二 · 三段顺序',
  ez:'“The order of the steps is fixed. Capture comes first. Then intermediate purification. Then polishing. That order is forced rather than chosen. Volume runs from large to small. The resolution you need runs from low to high. So the first column is picked for capacity. And the last one is picked for resolution.”',
  ezcn:'<b>步骤的顺序是：捕获 → 中度纯化 → 精修。</b><b>这个顺序是被逼出来的，不是挑出来的</b>：<b>体积从大到小，而你需要的分辨率从低到高</b>——<b>所以第一根柱子是按载量挑的，最后一根是按分辨率挑的。</b>',
  big:'先跑哪一根，问的不是「哪个方法好」，是<b>「样品现在有多大体积、有多脏」</b>',
  en:'“The order of the steps is capture, then intermediate purification, then polishing. That order is forced rather than chosen. Volume runs from large to small while the resolution you need runs from low to high. So the first column is picked for capacity and the last one is picked for resolution.”',
  note:'<span class="pg">L5 s.9</span>「顺序是被逼出来的、不是挑出来的」这一句笔记标了 beyond the slides，但它的根据在幻灯片上：SEC 的上样体积上限是柱体积的 5%，那是硬的。'},
 {n:'03', t:'没见过的模式怎么摆进去',
  ez:'“A chromatography mode is one property. It is the property the resin binds. Charge is one. Size is another. Suppose I meet a mode I have not seen before. Then I ask two questions. What property does the resin bind. And what do I change to release it. Those two answers put it into the four step frame. They also tell me roughly where in the order it belongs.”',
  ezcn:'<b>碰到一个没见过的层析模式，我问两个问题：树脂结合的是哪个性质？我改变什么才能把它放开？</b><b>这两个答案既把它放进那个四步框架，也大致告诉我它该排在顺序里的哪一段。</b>',
  big:'问两句就够：<b>它靠什么抓住？改什么它才放开？</b>',
  en:'“A chromatography mode is the one property the resin binds, such as charge or size. If I meet a mode I have not seen before, I ask two questions. What property does the resin bind, and what do I change to release it? Those two answers put it into the four-step frame and tell me roughly where in the order it belongs.”',
  note:'<b>这两句是这张卡自己排的，不是笔记上的句子。</b>但它们是从笔记的分类方式直接倒出来的——笔记那张「五种模式」的表，每一行就是「按什么分离」加「用什么洗脱」两栏。<span class="pg">L4 s.13</span><br>第三句可选：<b>容量和上样体积</b>决定它排在第几步。'},

 {g:'五种模式 · 按「抓什么 / 放什么」排', gn:'不是按名字背，是按<b>两栏</b>背。抓的那一栏是性质，放的那一栏是你手里的旋钮。'},
 {n:'04', t:'离子交换 IEX · 抓净电荷',
  big:'<b>缓冲液 pH 相对 pI</b> 决定抓不抓得住；<b>提高盐</b>让它放开',
  en:'“Ion exchange separates by overall charge and it needs no tag. One rule generates the whole table. Above its isoelectric point a protein is negative, and below it the protein is positive. An anion exchanger is itself positively charged, so it needs the protein negative, so you work above the pI. Elution raises the ionic strength, because salt ions shield the charges competitively.”',
  note:'树脂：<b>Q 和 DEAE 是阴离子交换</b>（自己带正电，抓带负电的蛋白，pH &gt; pI）；<b>SP 和 CM 是阳离子交换</b>（自己带负电，抓带正电的蛋白，pH &lt; pI）。电荷来自 <b>Arg / Lys</b>（正）和 <b>Asp / Glu</b>（负）——侧链那一格在卡 <b>aa</b>，pH 和 pI 本身在卡 <b>x-ph</b>。pI 可以用等电聚焦测，也可以用 Expasy ProtParam 从序列算。<span class="pg">L4 s.14–15</span><br>实践取 <b>pI ± 1 个 pH 单位</b>：太近电荷不够、结合太弱；太远杂蛋白也跟着上来。（这一条和下面那条笔记都标了 beyond the slides）',
  good:'加分的一句：盐梯度<b>自带分辨力</b>。盐离子竞争性地屏蔽电荷，所以结合最弱的先下来——梯度是边洗脱边分离，而不是一次性全放掉。',
  warn:'⚠ 最容易说反的一句。<b>阴离子交换剂自己带的是正电</b>，名字说的是它交换的离子，不是它自己的电荷。口诀：pH 比 pI 高 ＝ 环境偏碱 ＝ 质子被夺走 ＝ 蛋白「负」了。'},
 {n:'05', t:'疏水 HIC · 抓表面疏水性',
  big:'<b>高盐结合、低盐洗脱</b>——跟离子交换正好反过来',
  en:'“Hydrophobic interaction chromatography separates by the hydrophobicity of the protein surface. The salt conditions are the exact inverse of ion exchange. You bind at high salt and you elute at low salt. High salt pulls water away from the surface and strips the hydration shell. The hydrophobic patches are then forced into the open, and the resin can hold them.”',
  note:'结合 <b>1–2 M 醋酸铵</b>或 <b>3 M 氯化钠</b>，洗脱约 <b>50 mM 氯化钠</b>。树脂是丁基、己基、苯基琼脂糖，区别只在所接基团的疏水强弱。非极性残基：Ala、Val、Met、Leu、Ile、Phe、Trp。<span class="pg">L4 s.16</span><br>疏水效应这种相互作用本身在卡 <b>x-bonds</b>。',
  good:'这一条能顺势展示「你知道纯化是怎么设计的」：硫酸铵沉淀之后的样品<b>本来就是高盐</b>，可以直接上 HIC，一次缓冲液都不用换。如果下一步改成离子交换，就必须先脱盐。（笔记标 beyond the slides）'},
 {n:'06', t:'反相 RP · 同一个性质，变性的条件',
  big:'pH 2 的乙腈加 TFA。<b>分辨率极好，蛋白回不来了</b>',
  en:'“Reverse phase separates by the same property, hydrophobicity, on silica carrying C4, C8 or C18 alkyl chains. The mobile phase is a gradient of acetonitrile in water at pH 2 with 0.1 per cent trifluoroacetic acid. Those conditions are thoroughly denaturing. A short peptide has no tertiary structure to lose, so denaturation costs it nothing and it simply gains the resolution. A globular protein is destroyed by the run.”',
  note:'适合 <b>50 个氨基酸以内的短肽</b>、小分子有机物、寡核苷酸。定位是<b>分析</b>：纯度检定、质谱前处理，外加多肽制备。通常跑 HPLC，压力很高，所以要金属柱。<span class="pg">L4 s.17</span><br>「变性」这个词承重：什么条件能把蛋白打开、打开之后没了什么，在卡 <b>01</b>。',
  warn:'⚠ <b>HIC 和 RP 是同一个原理、相反的结局</b>，笔记自己写明这是标准的考试对比点。被问「有几种按疏水性分离的模式」，答两种，然后立刻说清差在条件不在原理。'},
 {n:'07', t:'分子排阻 SEC · 抓大小和形状',
  big:'<b>大分子先出来</b>，因为它们进不了孔，只能走珠子之间那条最短的路',
  en:'“Size exclusion separates by size and shape, and the largest molecules come out first. The beads are full of pores. A large molecule cannot enter them, so it travels only between the beads, and that is the shortest path available. A small molecule enters every pore, takes the long detour, and comes out last.”',
  note:'总体积 <code>Vt = V0 + Vg + Vi</code>：<b>V0</b> 珠子之间的空隙、<b>Vg</b> 树脂本身、<b>Vi</b> 孔道里的溶剂。<b>排阻极限</b>由孔径决定，超过它的分子全在 V0 一起出来、彼此分不开，所以选柱要按你关心的分子量：Superdex 75 是 3–70 kDa，Superdex 200 是 10–650 kDa，Superose 6 是 20–5000 kDa。四个用途：分开天然蛋白与聚集体、看纯度、换缓冲液、估寡聚状态（最后一项要校准柱）。<span class="pg">L5 s.5–7</span>',
  warn:'⚠ <b>两个陷阱叠在一格里。</b>第一，直觉会说「大分子更难穿过柱子所以最后出来」——正好反了。第二，<b>SEC 是四步框架唯一的例外</b>：它没有结合步，也没有洗脱步，样品上去之后一路走出来。<b>这一条是这张卡的推论，笔记里没有明说</b>，但笔记描述 SEC 时从头到尾没有 bind 和 elute，只有路径长短。被追问就这么说：分离靠的是路径，不是结合。'},
 {n:'08', t:'亲和层析 · 判据是二元的',
  big:'抓的是<b>特异结合</b>——问的是「<b>有没有</b>那个东西」，不是电荷大小疏水那种<b>程度差</b>',
  en:'“Affinity chromatography is the most widely used mode, because it is very specific and works in one step with high yields. The reason it can do in one step what the others need three steps for is that its criterion is binary. The resin asks whether the tag is there. It does not ask how much charge or how much hydrophobic surface a protein has. The price is that you usually have to add a tag to your own protein.”',
  note:'这个「二元 vs 程度差」的说法是这张卡的解释，<b>不是笔记的句子</b>；笔记给的是结论（特异性强、一步、产率高）。<span class="pg">L4 s.18–19</span><br>树脂谱：Ni-NTA、Streptactin、直链淀粉、谷胱甘肽琼脂糖、protein A/G、凝集素琼脂糖、链霉亲和素。<br>标签分两类：<b>短肽</b>（His 6–10 个组氨酸、Strep 的 WSHPQFEK、FLAG 的 DYKDDDDK）和<b>整个蛋白</b>（MBP 43 kDa、HALO 34 kDa、GST 26 kDa、硫氧还蛋白 12 kDa）。后一类还兼作溶解性标签。',
  good:'三条选标签的规矩（笔记标 beyond the slides）：① 要在<b>变性条件</b>下纯化 → 只能 His，因为别的都依赖折叠或蛋白–蛋白识别；② 蛋白<b>不溶</b> → 要 MBP 或硫氧还蛋白，His 只有六到十个残基，对溶解性毫无帮助；③ 要研究<b>寡聚状态</b> → 避开 GST，它自己会二聚。'},

 {g:'⚠ 三层 · 这张卡真正的任务', gn:'<b>结合 / 洗脱 / 移除。</b>三个问题听起来几乎一样，答案完全不同。丢分就丢在这三层混了。'},
 {n:'09', t:'第一层 · 结合（什么把它按住）',
  big:'His 标签的<b>咪唑侧链用氮原子配位</b>到 NTA 抓着的那个镍离子上',
  en:'“The histidine side chain is an imidazole ring, and it coordinates the nickel ion through its nitrogen atoms. The nickel itself is held on the resin by nitrilotriacetic acid, which is a chelating group. So the binding layer here is a coordination bond between the tag and a metal ion sitting on the resin.”',
  note:'<b>承重词，必须当场交代</b>：<b>配位键</b>＝把一对孤对电子送给金属离子形成的键。交代它是因为——它<b>不依赖蛋白折叠</b>，所以 Ni-NTA 在 <b>6 M 盐酸胍</b>里照样工作，而 MBP、GST、Strep 全部失效（它们认的是形状）。这就是包涵体那条变性路线基本只能用 His 标签的原因。<span class="pg">L4 s.20</span><br>各种键的分类在卡 <b>x-bonds</b>。Ni-NTA 容量约 <b>50 mg/mL 树脂</b>，是最常用的亲和树脂。',
  good:'别的标签的「第一层」各是什么，一句话一个：Strep 认的是改造过的链霉亲和素；FLAG 认的是单抗，而且<b>结合依赖钙离子</b>；MBP 认的是直链淀粉；GST 认的是谷胱甘肽；HALO 干脆是<b>共价</b>的。'},
 {n:'10', t:'第二层 · 洗脱（什么把它竞争下来）',
  big:'咪唑。<b>低浓度 20–40 mM 做洗涤，高浓度 250–500 mM 做洗脱</b>——同一个试剂，两种用法',
  en:'“Free imidazole is simply the bare version of that same side chain, so it competes for the nickel and displaces the tag. The wash buffer already contains 20 to 40 millimolar imidazole. That low concentration displaces host proteins that carry a few surface histidines by accident, while a real run of six histidines holds on. Elution then uses 250 to 500 millimolar. One reagent, two jobs, and the only difference between them is the concentration.”',
  note:'<span class="pg">L4 s.20</span> 数字是幻灯片上的；「为什么洗涤液里就已经有咪唑」这一条笔记标了 beyond the slides。<br><b>第二条洗脱路线是 pH：降到 5.6 以下。</b>机制不同——咪唑侧链的 pKa 约为 6，低于它侧链被质子化带正电，<b>失去了配位所需的那对孤对电子</b>。但酸会让蛋白变性，所以咪唑仍是首选。pKa 那一格在卡 <b>x-ph</b>。',
  warn:'⚠ <b>洗涤液里有咪唑不是加错了。</b>很多人看见这一步以为洗脱已经开始了。它恰恰是纯度的来源：Ni-NTA 的弱点就是会非特异地抓住表面带几个组氨酸的宿主蛋白，而低浓度咪唑正好把这些顶掉。'},
 {n:'11', t:'第二层的另一半 · 剥金属',
  big:'<b>螯合剂（EDTA）不是洗脱，是把镍整个抢走</b>。柱子变白，报废',
  en:'“There is a second thing that will take the protein off a nickel column, and it is not elution. EDTA is a chelator, so it strips the nickel ions off the resin altogether. The column turns white and it is finished. The trap is that EDTA is a routine lysis buffer component, added to inhibit metal-dependent proteases. DTT does the same damage by another route, because it reduces the nickel and then coordinates to it.”',
  note:'<span class="pg">L4 s.11–12</span> 幻灯片上写的是「Ni-NTA 不耐还原剂、不耐 EDTA」；为什么、以及「这两样都是标准裂解液成分」这个陷阱，笔记标了 beyond the slides。<br>所以上镍柱前必须换缓冲液，或者一开始就不加。蛋白确实需要还原环境时，<b>TCEP ≤1 mM</b> 相对可以耐受。<br>同样的逻辑：<b>Streptactin 怕生物素</b>，而昆虫和哺乳动物培养基里生物素浓度很高，会把位点占满，必须先透析。',
  warn:'⚠ <b>这是最漂亮的一个陷阱，因为同一句话在两根柱子上一个是操作、一个是事故。</b>EDTA 在 <b>FLAG 柱上就是正确的洗脱剂</b>，因为 M1 单抗的结合依赖钙离子，夺走钙就松手。在<b>镍柱上它是毁柱子</b>。所以「EDTA 能洗脱」这句话没有上下文就是错的。'},
 {n:'12', t:'第三层 · 移除（把标签从蛋白上切掉）',
  big:'蛋白酶。<b>另一台机器，为另一个理由做的，跟柱子没有关系</b>',
  en:'“Removal is a different operation done for a different reason. The tag can interfere with what you want to do next, so you cut it off with a protease. TEV recognises the sequence ENLYFQ and cuts before a glycine or a serine. PreScission recognises LEVLFQ and cuts before glycine proline. Neither of those has anything to do with getting the protein off a column.”',
  note:'选酶要权衡<b>成本、特异性、孵育时间、切割效率</b>。TEV 和 PreScission 占主导，很大一部分原因是<b>这两个都能在自己实验室里做出来</b>，几乎不要钱。<span class="pg">L5 s.8</span><br>切完还要把酶弄走：让蛋白酶自己带 His 标签，然后整管再过一次 Ni-NTA——<b>没切干净的融合蛋白和带标签的酶都留在柱上，不带标签的目标从穿透液出来</b>。这叫反向镍柱。丝氨酸蛋白酶也可以用苯甲脒琼脂糖抓走。',
  warn:'⚠ 幻灯片自己把 <b>Factor Xa</b> 和 <b>thrombin</b> 标成<b>非特异</b>（thrombin 一般会在精氨酸之后切）。它们会在你的目标蛋白内部误切、把它切碎。<b>被问「你会用哪个」，别报这两个的名字。</b>'},
 {n:'13', t:'⚠ 丢分就在这一格',
  big:'<b>「怎么中和 His 标签」问的是洗脱层</b>。答 imidazole。答 protease 是答到了移除层',
  en:'“Neutralising a tag and removing a tag are two different questions. Neutralising means getting the protein off the resin, and on a nickel column the answer is imidazole. Removing means cutting the tag off the protein with a protease. The first one happens on the column and the second one happens afterwards, in a tube.”',
  note:'听见问题先分层，判据是<b>三个动词的宾语不一样</b>：<br>· <b>hold</b> ——「什么把它按在树脂上」，宾语是<b>蛋白和树脂的关系</b>（配位键、静电、疏水、抗原抗体、共价）<br>· <b>release</b> ——「改什么条件让它松手」，宾语<b>还是那个关系</b>（咪唑、盐、pH、脱硫生物素、麦芽糖、谷胱甘肽、单糖）<br>· <b>cut</b> ——「把标签从蛋白上切掉」，宾语是<b>蛋白自己的肽链</b>（TEV、PreScission、SUMO 蛋白酶）<br><b>前两个在柱子上，第三个在管子里。</b>',
  warn:'⚠ <b>2026-09-01 这门课自己的口试上，这一处是丢分最重的一条。</b>他问的是中和（洗脱层），答的是切除（移除层）。<b>两个答案本身都对，但后一个不回答被问的那个问题。</b>他皱眉不是因为内容错，越改越远才是真正的损失。整条推理在 LOGIC 第 9 条。'},
 {n:'14', t:'而且「切掉」不等于「还原成原样」',
  big:'普通蛋白酶<b>留疤</b>：TEV 切完，你的蛋白 N 端永远多出一个甘氨酸',
  en:'“A sequence-recognising protease cuts inside a linear motif, so the residues downstream of the cut stay on your protein. After TEV your protein permanently begins with an extra glycine. SUMO protease is the one exception, because it recognises the three-dimensional fold of the SUMO domain instead of a sequence. It cuts exactly at the SUMO C-terminus and leaves a genuinely native N-terminus.”',
  note:'笔记把这一条标了 beyond the slides，幻灯片上只写了「SUMO 蛋白酶识别三级结构、给出天然 N 端、特异性 100%」。<span class="pg">L5 s.8</span><br>什么时候非要天然 N 端不可：N 端序列<b>本身有功能</b>时（信号肽、N 端规则、后续偶联要特定的 N 端残基），以及做结构生物学、不想要多余柔性残基时。SUMO 本身还是个不错的溶解性标签，一举两得，代价是酶比较贵。',
  good:'有一个标签自带切法：<b>FLAG 的 DDDDK 本身就是肠激酶的识别位点</b>，所以切掉它不需要另外设计一个切割位点。这条值得主动说，因为它把三层<b>在一个例子里</b>全串起来了：抗体抓住它、EDTA 或 3×FLAG 肽把它洗下来、肠激酶把它切掉。'},

 {g:'把三段顺序说完', gn:'顺序是这张卡的第二条骨架。<b>会说理由比会背规则值钱</b>，因为「SEC 为什么必须最后」是笔记点名的高频考点。'},
 {n:'15', t:'捕获 → 中度纯化 → 精修',
  big:'三段各自<b>为不同的东西</b>而选：先要容量，再要分辨率，最后要把杂的同类去掉',
  en:'“Capture pulls the target out of crude lysate in one step, and it is usually affinity. At that point the volume is large and the impurities are many, so what you need is capacity rather than resolution. Intermediate purification is ion exchange or hydrophobic interaction, and it removes contaminants with similar properties. Polishing is size exclusion. It removes aggregates and degradation fragments and sets the final storage buffer.”',
  note:'产率那一栏（幻灯片上的）：<b>高</b> ＝ 离子交换、Ni-NTA、疏水、protein A/G；<b>中</b> ＝ Streptactin、直链淀粉；<b>低</b> ＝ SEC 和 FLAG。另外三个选择标准是分辨率、通量（批式和磁珠是高通量形式）、时间（由流速和动态结合容量决定）。<span class="pg">L5 s.9</span>'},
 {n:'16', t:'为什么 SEC 只能排最后',
  big:'<b>上样体积不能超过柱体积的 5%</b> —— 这是硬的物理上限，不是习惯做法',
  en:'“Size exclusion has a hard constraint on it. The load volume must be under 5 per cent of the column volume, or the peaks broaden and the resolution collapses. You cannot put a litre of lysate onto a size exclusion column. Affinity handles large volumes, so affinity naturally leads and size exclusion naturally finishes.”',
  note:'第二个理由：SEC <b>顺带完成缓冲液置换</b>，直接把蛋白交到最终保存缓冲液里。收尾正好要这个效果。<br>第三条约束是<b>缓冲液状态的接力</b>：每一步留下的条件，下一步必须能接住。硫酸铵沉淀之后是高盐，HIC 直接能接，离子交换就得先脱盐。<b>设计顺序很大程度上就是在省掉不必要的缓冲液置换</b>，因为每换一次都费时间、也损失材料。（三条都标了 beyond the slides，但 5% 那个数在幻灯片上）'},
 {n:'17', t:'层析开始之前 · 样品先得够浓',
  big:'分泌表达的代价是<b>样品很稀</b>。大体积的标准手段是 <b>TFF（切向流过滤）</b>',
  en:'“Secretion gives you three things. You get N-glycosylated protein, purification is much simpler in serum-free media, and there is less protease contamination because the cell contents were never released. The cost is a dilute sample. Tangential flow filtration is the standard way to reduce tens of litres before any chromatography can start.”',
  note:'另一个办法是<b>硫酸铵沉淀</b>，它本身就算一个纯化步骤，但工业规模上需要的量大到不现实。<span class="pg">L4 s.5–6</span><br>TFF 又叫超滤：液体在压力差下<b>平行掠过</b>半透膜，进料分成<b>截留液</b>（被拦下的，你的蛋白在这里）和<b>透过液</b>。跟普通死端过滤的区别只有一条——死端过滤里液体垂直冲向膜，被截留的分子堆成滤饼、很快把膜堵死；平行流持续把膜面刷干净。（这条对比笔记标了 beyond the slides）'},

 {g:'收尾 · 纯度和浓度', gn:'「纯化完了」这句话要有两个数才站得住：<b>一块胶</b>和<b>一个浓度</b>。'},
 {n:'18', t:'纯度 · SDS-PAGE',
  big:'SDS <b>同时干了三件事</b>，三件合起来，迁移率才只剩分子量这一个变量',
  en:'“SDS does three separate jobs. It denatures the protein and unfolds it into a linear chain. It binds at roughly one molecule per two residues, so its own negative charge overwhelms the protein and every protein ends with the same charge to mass ratio. And it makes everything rod-shaped, so shape stops mattering. Only molecular weight is left to vary.”',
  note:'这就是为什么叫 <b>SDS</b>-PAGE 而不只是 PAGE：天然电泳里迁移率同时受电荷、大小、形状三样影响，读不出分子量。<br><b>还原剂是第四个、独立的要素</b>——DTT 或 β-巯基乙醇打断二硫键。不加就是<b>非还原胶</b>，用来看有没有分子间二硫键：抗体在还原胶上分成重链和轻链两条带，在非还原胶上是一条 150 kDa 的带。<br>染色：考马斯 <b>50–100 ng</b>，银染 <b>1–5 ng</b>（灵敏 10–50 倍，但定量性差、操作繁琐）。步骤：混样、<b>煮 5 分钟</b>、跑、染。<span class="pg">L5 s.11</span>（三件事和非还原胶标了 beyond the slides）'},
 {n:'19', t:'浓度 · A280 为什么不用标准曲线',
  big:'<code>c = A₂₈₀ / (ε·l)</code>；<b>ε 能从序列算出来</b>，所以不用曲线——这是它跟 Bradford 的根本差别',
  en:'“A 280 works because the extinction coefficient can be calculated from the sequence. Tryptophan absorbs most at 280 nanometres, then tyrosine, with phenylalanine far behind. So you count those residues instead of building a standard curve. Bradford needs a curve, because the dye binds mainly basic and aromatic residues and different proteins respond very differently.”',
  note:'<b>=== 公式和推导（背之前先看懂这一段） ===</b><br><b>式子</b>：<code>A = ε · c · l</code>（Beer–Lambert）<br>A 是吸光度，没有单位 · ε 是摩尔消光系数，单位 <code>M⁻¹cm⁻¹</code> · c 是摩尔浓度，单位 <code>M</code> · l 是光程，单位 <code>cm</code>。<br><br><b>四步推导</b>（他问「为什么吸光度能当浓度用」就照这个说）：<br>① 光每走一小段 <code>dx</code>，被吸掉的<b>比例</b>正比于路上的分子数：<code>−dI/I = k·c·dx</code>。<b>关键在「比例」两个字</b>——吸收是按比例削减，不是按定量削减。<br>② 从 0 积到 l：<code>ln(I₀/I) = k·c·l</code>。<b>这就是为什么会出现对数。</b><br>③ 换成以 10 为底，把常数并进 ε：<code>A = log₁₀(I₀/I) = ε·c·l</code>。<br>④ 反解，标准比色皿 <code>l = 1 cm</code>：<code>c = A₂₈₀ / ε</code>；要 mg/mL 就再乘分子量 <code>M</code>（g/mol）→ <code>c(mg/mL) = A₂₈₀ · M / ε</code>。<br><br><b>=== 一句话理解 ===</b><br><b>A280 是在「数色氨酸」，Bradford 是在「数碱性和芳香族残基，再拿去跟 BSA 比」。</b>前者的标尺长在<b>你自己的序列</b>上，ProtParam 一按就有；后者的标尺长在<b>别人的蛋白</b>上。所以前者不需要曲线，后者必须做曲线，而且换一个蛋白、曲线就不一定还对——笔记说拿 BSA 曲线去测富含酸性残基的蛋白，可能差好几倍。<br>⚠ <b>Beer–Lambert 的这套积分推导是通用物理化学，课上没给</b>；幻灯片给的是「消光系数可以从序列得到」这一句和各方法的取舍。消光系数由 Trp、Tyr 和胱氨酸含量算出，这一条在笔记的术语表里。',
  warn:'⚠ <b>A280 的两处失效，都要能当场说。</b>① <b>核酸在 260–280 nm 也强吸收</b>，粗样品会被严重高估——查 <b>A260/A280</b> 比值，纯蛋白应约 <b>0.57</b>，偏高就是 DNA 或 RNA 在抬读数。② <b>不含色氨酸的蛋白</b>消光系数极低，这个数测出来没有意义。',
  good:'三条实用规则收尾：<b>纯蛋白用 A280</b>（快、不耗样、不用曲线）；<b>粗样品或含核酸的用 Bradford</b>（灵敏到 1 µg，不受核酸干扰，但怕 SDS 和 Triton）；<b>有还原剂时不要用 BCA 或 Lowry</b>，铜化学会被还原剂破坏。'}
],
end:'<b>四步是框架，三段是顺序，三层是不许混的那三个问题。</b>开口之前先在心里确认一句：<b>他问的是哪一层？</b>',

sib:[
['<b>四步</b>：平衡 → 结合 → 洗涤 → 洗脱。所有模式共用，区别只在「靠什么结合」',
 '“Every mode runs the same four steps. Equilibrate, bind, wash, elute. What changes between modes is only the property being exploited.”',
 '<b>整张卡的骨架。</b>先给这一句，他后面无论问哪个模式，你都已经有位置放它了。'],
['<b>模式只有五种</b>：电荷 · 特异结合 · 大小和形状 · 疏水（两种）',
 '“Five modes. Ion exchange by charge, affinity by specific binding, size exclusion by size and shape, and two by hydrophobicity. Those last two are hydrophobic interaction and reverse phase.”',
 '「疏水那一栏有两个」本身就是考点。笔记说这是<b>标准的考试对比</b>：同一个原理，一个保住构象、一个彻底变性。'],
['<b>IEX</b>：pH &gt; pI 蛋白带负电 → 上阴离子交换（Q、DEAE）；<b>提高盐</b>洗脱',
 '“Above its isoelectric point a protein is negative. An anion exchanger is positively charged, so it needs the protein negative, so you work above the pI. You elute by raising the ionic strength.”',
 '一条规则推出整张表。<b>别去背表。</b>pI 本身在卡 <b>x-ph</b>，带电侧链在卡 <b>aa</b>。'],
['<b>HIC</b>：<b>高盐结合、低盐洗脱</b>，跟 IEX 正好反过来',
 '“Hydrophobic interaction binds at high salt and elutes at low salt. High salt strips the hydration shell, so the hydrophobic patches are exposed to the resin.”',
 '最容易说反的一条。记「盐屏蔽电荷、盐夺走水」，两个方向就不会乱。'],
['<b>SEC</b>：大分子<b>先</b>出来；上样 &lt; 柱体积 5%，所以永远最后',
 '“The largest molecules come out first, because they cannot enter the pores and travel only between the beads. The load volume must be under 5 per cent of the column volume, so it is always the last step.”',
 '两个高频考点挤在一格里：<b>为什么大的先出来</b>，和<b>为什么必须最后</b>。'],
['<b>Ni-NTA</b>：组氨酸的咪唑侧链<b>配位</b>镍；咪唑竞争下来',
 '“The histidine side chain coordinates the nickel through its nitrogen atoms. Free imidazole is the bare version of that side chain, so it competes and displaces the tag.”',
 '说出「<b>咪唑就是组氨酸侧链本身</b>」，洗脱机制就不用另外背了，它自己解释自己。'],
['<b>20–40 mM 洗涤 · 250–500 mM 洗脱</b>：同一个试剂，差别只在浓度',
 '“The wash already contains 20 to 40 millimolar imidazole, which removes host proteins carrying a few surface histidines. Elution uses 250 to 500 millimolar.”',
 '<b>洗涤液里有咪唑不是加错了</b>，它正是纯度的来源。'],
['⚠ <b>中和 ≠ 切除</b>：中和在洗脱层（咪唑），切除在移除层（蛋白酶）',
 '“Neutralising the tag means getting the protein off the resin, and that is imidazole. Removing the tag means cutting it off with a protease. Those are two different questions.”',
 '<b>这是 2026-09-01 丢分最重的一处。</b>两个答案都对，但后一个没有回答被问的那个问题。'],
['<b>EDTA 不是洗脱</b>：它是螯合剂，把镍整个剥走，柱子报废',
 '“EDTA is a chelator, so it strips the nickel off the resin and the column is finished. And EDTA is a routine lysis buffer component, which is what makes it a real trap.”',
 '同一个 EDTA 在 <b>FLAG 柱上却是正确的洗脱剂</b>，因为那里的结合依赖钙离子。<b>脱离柱子谈试剂没有意义。</b>'],
['<b>顺序</b>：捕获 → 中度纯化 → 精修；体积从大到小，分辨率从低到高',
 '“Capture, intermediate purification, polishing. The order is forced rather than chosen, because volume runs from large to small while the resolution you need runs from low to high.”',
 '<b>「forced rather than chosen」这个说法本身就值分</b>，它表明你知道这不是约定俗成。'],
['<b>纯度和浓度</b>：SDS-PAGE 看纯度，A280 看浓度（ε 从序列算，不用曲线）',
 '“Purity is assessed by SDS-PAGE and concentration by absorbance at 280 nanometres. No standard curve is needed there, because the extinction coefficient can be calculated from the sequence.”',
 '「纯化完了」这句话要有两个数才站得住。<b>核酸在 280 也吸收</b>，所以粗样品别用 A280。']
],

segs:[
 {tag:'段 1 · 定义', h:'先把「层析」这个词和那四步摆上桌，再说模式只是名字',
  p:['“Purification means taking one protein out of everything else that came out of the cell, and the main tool is chromatography. Chromatography separates the components of a mixture using a mobile phase that flows through a fixed porous stationary phase. The mobile phase is the buffer that carries the components along. The stationary phase is a solid that stays put, normally a porous resin, a membrane or a gel.”',
      '“The useful thing is that every mode runs the same four steps. You equilibrate the resin, bind the target, wash the contaminants away, then elute the target. What differs between modes is only which property of the protein is being exploited. That property decides what you have to change in order to let it go. So a mode is really just an answer to two questions: what does the resin bind, and what releases it?”'],
  note:'<b>为什么从这里起步</b>：老师默认技术名词你已经知道，所以答案必须从定义开始（LOGIC 第 2 条）。而「流动相」「固定相」两个词<b>承重</b>——不交代它们，「层析」就只是个名字。<br>组分标签：INJ 上样 · FT 穿透液 · W 洗涤 · E 洗脱 · C 清洗，洗涤和洗脱各约 10 个柱体积。<span class="pg">L4 s.8–10</span><br>柱式和批式的区别也在这一节：柱式分辨率最好；批式（烧杯或离心管里混，离心或磁铁回收）适合<b>动态结合容量低</b>的树脂和高通量。'},
 {tag:'段 2 · general', h:'五种模式按两栏排开，顺便把「先跑哪一根」也一起答掉',
  p:['“There are five modes, and I would sort them by the property each one binds. Ion exchange binds overall charge, and you release it by raising the salt. Hydrophobic interaction binds surface hydrophobicity, and you release it by lowering the salt. Reverse phase binds the same property but in acetonitrile at pH 2, so it releases by organic solvent and denatures everything on the way. Affinity binds a specific partner, and you release it with a competitor. Size exclusion binds nothing at all, and that is why it has no elution step.”',
      '“Which one comes first is a separate question, and it is answered by capture, intermediate purification and polishing. Capture takes the target out of crude lysate in one step, and it is usually affinity, because at that point the volume is large and what you need is capacity. Intermediate purification is ion exchange or hydrophobic interaction, and it removes contaminants with similar properties. Polishing is size exclusion. The order is forced rather than chosen, because volume runs from large to small while the resolution you need runs from low to high.”'],
  note:'<b>第二段是这张卡的主承重段。</b>它同时回答「有哪些」和「什么顺序」，而且两个答案用的是同一个逻辑：<b>按性质排，不按名字排。</b><br>⚠ <b>「Size exclusion binds nothing at all」是这张卡的推论，笔记没有这么写。</b>笔记说所有模式都是四步，又在讲 SEC 时从头到尾没有 bind 和 elute。被追问就说判据：SEC 分离靠的是<b>路径长短</b>，不是结合，所以它本来就不在那个框架里。<b>说出这个例外比背那个框架更像研究者。</b><br>顺序那一段的硬根据是 SEC 的 <b>5% 柱体积</b>上样上限。<span class="pg">L4 s.13 · L5 s.9</span>'},
 {tag:'段 3 · 稍展开', h:'三层分开说。这一段是这张卡存在的理由',
  p:['“I want to separate three things that sound alike, because a question about a tag can be about any one of them. The first is binding: what holds the tag on the resin. For a histidine tag the side chain is an imidazole ring, and it coordinates a nickel ion held on the resin by nitrilotriacetic acid. That is a coordination bond, and it does not depend on the protein being folded, which is why a nickel column still works in 6 M guanidinium.”',
      '“The second is elution: what competes the tag off. Free imidazole is the bare version of that same side chain, so it competes for the nickel. The wash already contains 20 to 40 millimolar, which removes host proteins that carry a few surface histidines. Elution uses 250 to 500. There is also a chelator, EDTA, and a chelator does something different. It strips the nickel off the resin and kills the column, and it is a routine lysis buffer component, so it is a real hazard rather than an option.”',
      '“The third is removal: cutting the tag off the protein with a protease, and that is done for a different reason. You remove a tag because it interferes with what you want to do next, not because you want the protein off the column. TEV and PreScission are the usual choices, and both can be made in the lab. The first two layers happen on the column. The third happens afterwards, in a tube.”'],
  note:'<b>这一段存在的全部理由</b>：2026-09-01 那场口试上，他问「怎么中和 His 标签」，答案在<b>洗脱层</b>（咪唑竞争配位），她答在<b>移除层</b>（蛋白酶切位点）。两个答案本身都对，但后一个<b>不回答被问的那个问题</b>。LOGIC 第 9 条。<br><b>所以这三段不能压缩成一段。</b>说的时候用三个动词把它们钉住：<b>hold · release · cut</b>。前两个的宾语是「蛋白和树脂的关系」，第三个的宾语是「蛋白自己的肽链」。<br>⚠ 还要补一句以防他再问下去：<b>切掉不等于还原成原样。</b>TEV 切完 N 端永远多一个甘氨酸；只有 SUMO 蛋白酶留下天然 N 端，因为它认的是三维结构、切在结构域末端。<span class="pg">L4 s.20 · L5 s.8</span>'},
 {tag:'段 4 · 留口子', h:'亲和树脂其实是一台 Kd 机器 —— 主动把话题引到自己的地盘',
  p:['“The thing an affinity resin actually exploits is a dissociation constant. The resin presents a ligand, and the target has a small K d for it while the host proteins have large ones. A wash works when there is a gap between those two numbers. That is why the wash is the step that decides purity, and not the elution.”',
      '“Streptavidin and biotin show what happens when that gap is pushed to its limit. The dissociation constant is 10 to the minus 15 molar. That is among the tightest non-covalent interactions known. You can wash under very harsh conditions and lose nothing. But you also cannot get the protein off again, so the advantage and the liability are one fact rather than two.”',
      '“There are two ways out, and both are design decisions rather than accidents. Either you engineer the affinity down, and the Strep system is exactly that. Streptactin is a modified streptavidin with deliberately lowered biotin affinity, and it elutes mildly with desthiobiotin. Or you do not elute at all, and you keep the protein on the beads for the next experiment.”',
      '“That is also where this connects to my own work, because the same number governs both halves of it. A dissociation constant tells you whether a wash will keep your protein on a column. It also tells you whether a displayed variant is worth selecting. A selection and a wash are the same operation, run for different reasons.”'],
  note:'<b>这一段是故意留的口子</b>（LOGIC 第 4 条）：你不给他抓手，他自己会去挑一个深坑。Kd 是她的主场，完整的一张卡在 <b>02</b>。<br><b>=== 公式和推导（洗涤为什么能只冲掉杂蛋白） ===</b><br><b>式子</b>：<code>f = [R] / ([R] + K<sub>d</sub>)</code><br>f 是目标蛋白<b>留在树脂上的比例</b> · [R] 是树脂上<b>有效配体浓度</b>（每毫升树脂上那些镍位点的等效浓度） · K<sub>d</sub> 是这一对的解离常数，单位是浓度。<br><br><b>四步推导</b>：<br>① 结合平衡写成 <code>P + R ⇌ PR</code>，按卡 <b>02</b> 的定义 <code>K<sub>d</sub> = [P][R] / [PR]</code>。<br>② 整理得 <code>[PR]/[P] = [R]/K<sub>d</sub></code>——<b>「抓住的」对「游离的」之比，只由 [R] 和 K<sub>d</sub> 的比值决定。</b><br>③ 留在树脂上的比例 <code>f = [PR]/([P]+[PR])</code>，上下同除 [P] → <code>f = [R]/([R]+K<sub>d</sub>)</code>。<br>④ 把<b>同一个 [R]</b> 代进两个不同的 Kd：目标 Kd 很小 → f≈1，几乎全留；杂蛋白 Kd 很大 → f≈0，几乎全走。<b>洗涤窗口就是 [R] 落在这两个 Kd 之间的那一段。</b><br><br><b>竞争洗脱是同一条曲线上往右挪</b>：加入浓度 [I] 的咪唑，表观解离常数变成 <code>K<sub>d</sub>′ = K<sub>d</sub>(1 + [I]/K<sub>I</sub>)</code>。[I] 越高，K<sub>d</sub>′ 越大，f 越小。<b>20–40 mM 把弱结合的杂蛋白推过阈值，250–500 mM 把 His 标签自己也推过去。</b><br><br><b>=== 一句话理解 ===</b><br><b>洗涤和洗脱不是两件事，是同一条曲线上的两个点。</b>你从头到尾在做同一个动作——把有效的 Kd 往上抬——区别只是抬多少。<b>而「切掉标签」根本不在这条曲线上</b>：它不改变任何 Kd，它改变的是那条肽链。<b>这句话就是三层分开的数学版本。</b><br>⚠ <b>这套占据率推导和竞争公式，课上没给，笔记里也没有</b>，是通用的结合热力学（卡 <b>02</b> 用的是同一套）。被追出处就说 “that is the general binding equilibrium, not something from the course.”。幻灯片给的只是那几个浓度数字和「咪唑竞争配位」这一句。<br>另一个可换的数：Kd 每小十倍，结合自由能约多 <b>5.71 kJ/mol</b>（25 °C 的 RT·ln10）——<b>这也是通用热力学，不是课上的数</b>，卡 <b>02</b> 和卡 <b>x-bonds</b> 用的是同一个。'}
],

why:{
 rungs:[
  ['为什么每一种模式都是那四步？','因为每一种做的其实是<b>同一件事</b>：让目标粘在某个东西上、而杂质不粘，然后<b>只改一个条件</b>把它放开。模式的名字只是在回答「粘的是哪个性质」。<b>四步不是流程规定，是这个想法的最短实现。</b>'],
  ['那为什么决定纯度的是洗涤，不是洗脱？','因为<b>洗脱一视同仁</b>——条件改到那一步，谁在上面谁就下来。真正做区分的是<b>洗涤</b>：停在「目标还抓得住、杂质已经抓不住」的那个条件上，多冲几个柱体积。而这个条件窗口由<b>两个 K<sub>d</sub> 之间的差</b>决定（卡 <b>02</b>）。<b>所以纯度是在洗涤里挣来的。</b>'],
  ['那为什么最后还要跑一根 SEC，前面明明已经很纯了？','因为前面每一步区分的都是「<b>跟目标不一样</b>的东西」，而聚集体和降解片段<b>跟目标是同一个序列</b>——电荷一样、疏水性一样、标签也一样，前面所有柱子都分不开它们。<b>只剩一个性质还不一样：大小。</b>'],
  ['那为什么不干脆一直洗、一直提高严格度，直到只剩目标？','因为<b>目标自己也在那条曲线上</b>。把条件推到杂质全掉光，目标也开始掉。这是一个<b>产率和纯度之间的取舍</b>，不是一个可以靠更努力解决的问题。']
 ],
 stop:{lbl:'停 · 落在「测量方法的限制」',
  say:'“And below that, the word pure stops being a property of the sample. It becomes a statement about what the assay can see. Coomassie detects about 50 to 100 nanograms and silver detects about 1 to 5. A band that is absent on one gel can be present on the other.”'}
},

recog:[
{q:'How do you purify a protein?',
  ez:'“Purification means taking one protein out. It comes out of everything else the cell contained. The main tool is chromatography. Every mode runs the same four steps. Equilibrate. Bind. Wash. Elute. Only one thing differs between modes. It is which property is exploited. There are five modes. They sort by that property. Charge. Specific binding. Size and shape. And hydrophobicity.”',
  ezcn:'<b>纯化 ＝ 把一个蛋白从细胞里其余一切东西中取出来，主要工具是层析。</b><b>每一种模式跑同样的四步：平衡 → 结合 → 洗 → 洗脱。</b><b>模式之间唯一的差别是「利用哪个性质」。</b><b>一共五种模式，按性质排：电荷 · 专一结合 · 大小和形状 · 疏水性。</b>',
 mean:'<b>最短的问法。</b>他不会替你把题目问完整。答案要自带结构：<b>定义 → 四步 → 挑哪几个模式 → 什么顺序</b>。',
 say:'“Purification means taking one protein out of everything else the cell contained, and the main tool is chromatography. Every mode runs the same four steps: equilibrate, bind, wash, elute. What differs between modes is only which property is being exploited. There are five modes, sorted by that property: charge, specific binding, size and shape, and hydrophobicity, which covers two of them. And the order is capture, intermediate purification, polishing, because volume runs from large to small while the resolution you need runs from low to high.”',
 tail:'说完这一段，他手里所有能问的方向你都已经命名过了。<b>然后停。</b>'},
{q:'How do you neutralise a histidine tag?',
  ez:'“You compete it off with imidazole. The histidine side chain is an imidazole ring. That ring coordinates the nickel. So free imidazole is the bare version of that side chain. It displaces the tag. Elution is at two hundred and fifty to five hundred millimolar. The wash already contains twenty to forty. That removes host proteins. Those carry a few surface histidines.”',
  ezcn:'<b>用咪唑把它竞争下来。</b><b>组氨酸的侧链就是一个咪唑环，它配位镍——所以游离咪唑是那个侧链的光杆版本，能把标签顶下来。</b><b>洗脱用 250–500 mM；洗涤液里本来就有 20–40 mM，用来去掉那些碰巧表面带几个组氨酸的宿主蛋白。</b>',
 mean:'⚠ <b>实测题，而且是丢分最重的那一处。</b>他问的是<b>洗脱层</b>。答 imidazole。',
 say:'“You compete it off with imidazole. The histidine side chain is an imidazole ring that coordinates the nickel, so free imidazole is the bare version of that side chain and displaces the tag. Elution is at 250 to 500 millimolar. The wash already contains 20 to 40, which is there to remove host proteins that carry a few surface histidines.”',
 tail:'<b>2026-09-01 答成了 protease，那是移除层。</b>两个答案都对，但后一个不回答被问的那个问题。<b>听见 neutralise、elute、release、get it off the column，都是同一层。</b>'},
{q:'How do you take the tag off afterwards?',
  ez:'“With a protease. T E V recognises E N L Y F Q. It cuts before a glycine or a serine. PreScission recognises L E V L F Q. It cuts before glycine proline. Both can be produced in the lab. That is why they are the default. Then you have to remove the protease itself. The neat way uses a His tagged protease. You pass everything back over nickel. The protease binds. So does uncleaved fusion. The cut protein flows through.”',
  ezcn:'<b>用蛋白酶。</b><b>TEV 识别 ENLYFQ，在甘氨酸或丝氨酸前切；PreScission 识别 LEVLFQ，在甘氨酸-脯氨酸前切</b>；<b>两者都能在实验室自己表达，所以成了默认选择</b>。<b>之后还得把蛋白酶本身去掉——漂亮的做法是用带 His 标签的蛋白酶，把所有东西再过一遍镍柱：蛋白酶和没切开的融合蛋白都挂住，切好的目标蛋白流出来。</b>',
 mean:'<b>这才是移除层。</b>同一个话题的另一个问题，答案完全不同。',
 say:'“With a protease. TEV recognises ENLYFQ and cuts before a glycine or a serine, and PreScission recognises LEVLFQ and cuts before glycine proline. Both can be produced in the lab, which is why they are the default. Then you have to remove the protease itself, and the neat way is to use a His-tagged protease and pass everything back over nickel. The protease binds, uncleaved fusion binds, and your tag-free target comes out in the flow-through.”',
 tail:'⚠ 顺手补一句：<b>切掉不等于还原成原样。</b>TEV 留一个甘氨酸在 N 端；只有 SUMO 蛋白酶给天然 N 端，因为它认的是三维结构。'},
{q:'Why is there imidazole in the wash buffer already?',
  ez:'“Because washing and eluting differ only in concentration. Some host proteins carry a few surface histidines by accident. They bind weakly. Twenty to forty millimolar displaces exactly those. A real run of six histidines holds on. Then two hundred and fifty to five hundred takes the tag itself off. One reagent is doing two jobs.”',
  ezcn:'因为<b>洗涤和洗脱的差别只在浓度上</b>。<b>有些宿主蛋白碰巧表面带几个组氨酸，结合得弱；20–40 mM 正好把那些顶下来，而真正的六聚组氨酸还挂得住</b>；<b>然后 250–500 mM 才把标签本身带下来。</b><b>同一种试剂在干两件事。</b>',
 mean:'他在测你知不知道<b>洗涤和洗脱是同一个连续量</b>。答浓度差，别答「洗涤和洗脱是两个东西」。',
 say:'“Because the difference between washing and eluting is only the concentration. Some host proteins carry a few surface histidines by accident and bind weakly. 20 to 40 millimolar displaces exactly those, while a real run of six histidines holds on. Then 250 to 500 takes the tag itself off. One reagent doing two jobs.”',
 tail:'这一条顺势能接到卡 <b>02</b>：弱结合和强结合的分界，就是两个 K<sub>d</sub> 之间的那段窗口。'},
{q:'Which column would you run first, and why?',
  ez:'“Affinity first. Normally that is nickel or protein A. The reason is not that affinity is best. At that point the volume is large. The impurities are many. So what you need is capacity. Resolution is not what you need yet. Resolution is worth chasing later. It is worth it once the volume is small.”',
  ezcn:'<b>先跑亲和</b>（<b>通常是镍柱或 protein A</b>）。<b>理由不是「亲和最好」</b>：<b>那一步体积大、杂质多，所以你要的是载量，不是分辨率</b>。<b>分辨率要等体积变小之后再去追。</b>',
 mean:'他要的是<b>判据</b>，不是某个方法的名字。答体积和容量。',
 say:'“Affinity first, normally nickel or protein A. The reason is not that affinity is the best method. It is that at that point the volume is large and the impurities are many, so what you need is capacity rather than resolution. Resolution is worth chasing later, once the volume is small.”',
 tail:'<b>「不是因为它最好，是因为样品现在是那个样子」</b>——这一句本身就是这道题的骨架。'},
{q:'Why must size exclusion chromatography be last?',
  ez:'“Because the load volume must be small. It must be under five per cent of the column volume. Otherwise the peaks broaden. And the resolution collapses. You cannot put a litre of lysate on such a column. That is a hard physical limit. It is not a convention. There is a second reason too. Size exclusion exchanges the buffer as a side effect. So it delivers the protein into its final storage buffer.”',
  ezcn:'因为<b>上样体积必须很小——小于柱体积的 5%</b>，<b>否则峰变宽、分辨率崩掉</b>。<b>一升裂解液根本放不上去。这是物理上的硬限制，不是约定。</b><b>还有第二个理由：分子筛顺带就把缓冲液换掉了，于是它直接把蛋白送进最终的保存缓冲液里。</b>',
 mean:'笔记点名的<b>高频考点</b>。要给<b>理由</b>，不要只给规则。',
 say:'“Because the load volume must be under 5 per cent of the column volume, or the peaks broaden and the resolution collapses. You cannot put a litre of lysate onto a size exclusion column. That is a hard physical limit rather than a convention. There is a second reason too. Size exclusion exchanges the buffer as a side effect, so it delivers the protein straight into its final storage conditions.”',
 tail:'第三条理由更深：聚集体和降解片段<b>跟目标是同一个序列</b>，所以只有按大小才分得开。这一条放在 why 里。'},
{q:'I name a resin you have never used. Where does it go in a purification?',
  ez:'“I have not used that one. But I can place it by asking two questions. What property does the resin bind? And what do I change to release it? Those two answers put it into the four step frame. Then two more things tell me the position. Capacity and permissible load volume do. They tell me whether it belongs at capture, in the middle, or at polishing.”',
  ezcn:'<b>那个我没用过，但我可以靠两个问题把它安放好：树脂结合的是哪个性质？我改变什么才能把它放开？</b><b>这两个答案把它放进那个四步框架。</b><b>然后载量和允许的上样体积告诉我它的位置：该放在捕获、中段，还是精修。</b>',
 mean:'他在测<b>框架</b>，不是测覆盖。<b>承认没见过，然后当场把它安放好。</b>',
 say:'“I have not used that one, but I can place it by asking two questions. What property does the resin bind, and what do I change to release it? Those two answers put it into the four-step frame. Then capacity and permissible load volume tell me whether it belongs at capture, in the middle, or at polishing.”',
 tail:'<b>这比背出一百个树脂名字都值分。</b>「我没用过」后面接一个判据，是研究者的回答；接一个猜测，是学生的回答。'},
{q:'What is the difference between HIC and reverse phase?',
  ez:'“They separate by the same property. That property is hydrophobicity. The difference is the conditions. Hydrophobic interaction runs in aqueous buffer. It runs at high salt. So the protein stays folded. The method is genuinely preparative. Reverse phase runs in acetonitrile. It runs at p H two with trifluoroacetic acid. That is thoroughly denaturing. So reverse phase is for analysis. It also suits short peptides.”',
  ezcn:'<b>两者按同一个性质分离：疏水性。差别在条件。</b><b>疏水作用层析在水相缓冲液、高盐下跑，蛋白保持折叠，所以它是真正可用于制备的</b>。<b>反相在乙腈、pH 2、加三氟乙酸的条件下跑，那是彻底变性的</b>——<b>所以反相用于分析，以及短肽。</b>',
 mean:'笔记自己说这是<b>标准的考试对比</b>。差别不在原理，在条件。',
 say:'“They separate by the same property, hydrophobicity. The difference is the conditions. Hydrophobic interaction runs in aqueous buffer at high salt, so the protein stays folded and the method is genuinely preparative. Reverse phase runs in acetonitrile at pH 2 with trifluoroacetic acid, which is thoroughly denaturing. So reverse phase is for analysis and for short peptides, and it is not a way to recover functional protein.”',
 tail:'为什么短肽不在乎变性：<b>它没有三级结构可以失去</b>。什么是三级结构，在卡 <b>01</b>。'},
{q:'How do you know when the protein is pure enough?',
  ez:'“By S D S P A G E. You stain it with Coomassie or with silver. But pure is not really a property of the sample. It is a statement about the assay. It says what the assay can see. Coomassie detects about fifty to one hundred nanograms. Silver detects about one to five. So a band absent on one gel can be present on the other. Pure enough must mean pure enough for the next experiment.”',
  ezcn:'<b>靠 SDS-PAGE，用考马斯亮蓝或银染。</b>⚠ <b>但「纯」其实不是样品的属性，而是关于检测方法的一句话——它说的是「这个方法看得见什么」</b>：<b>考马斯的检测限约 50–100 ng，银染约 1–5 ng</b>；<b>一条在这张胶上不存在的带，在另一张上可能存在</b>。<b>「够纯」只能意味着「对你接下来要做的实验够纯」。</b>',
 mean:'他要的是<b>判据加上判据的边界</b>。这一条能直接走到停止句。',
 say:'“By SDS-PAGE, stained with Coomassie or with silver. But pure is not really a property of the sample. It is a statement about what the assay can see. Coomassie detects about 50 to 100 nanograms and silver about 1 to 5. So a band that is absent on one gel can be present on the other, and pure enough has to mean pure enough for the experiment you are about to do.”',
 tail:'<b>这是这张卡的停止句。</b>它落在「测量方法的限制」那块地基上。'},
{q:'How would you purify a protein that refuses to dissolve?',
  ez:'“There are two routes. The first purifies it under denaturing conditions. It purifies from inclusion bodies. That route commits you to a histidine tag. Nickel binding is a coordination bond. It survives six molar guanidinium. M B P, G S T and Strep all depend on a fold instead. The second route makes the protein soluble first. A large soluble fusion partner does that. M B P is forty three kilodaltons.”',
  ezcn:'<b>两条路。</b><b>① 在变性条件下从包涵体里纯化</b>——<b>这条路把你锁死在 His 标签上，因为镍结合是配位键，能扛住 6 M 盐酸胍；而 MBP、GST、Strep 都依赖一个折叠好的结构。</b><b>② 一开始就让蛋白可溶</b>——<b>用一个大的可溶融合伴侣，比如 43 kDa 的 MBP。</b>',
 mean:'两条路，而且选标签的规矩<b>在这里被逼出来</b>。',
 say:'“Two routes. The first is to purify it under denaturing conditions from inclusion bodies. That route commits you to a histidine tag, because nickel binding is a coordination bond that survives 6 M guanidinium. MBP and GST and Strep all depend on a fold instead. The second route is to make the protein soluble in the first place, with a large soluble fusion partner. MBP is 43 kilodaltons and thioredoxin is 12. A histidine tag cannot do that job, because 6 to 10 residues do nothing for solubility.”',
 tail:'常见解法是<b>双标签 His-MBP</b>：镍柱靠容量抓总量，切掉标签，再用反向镍柱去掉没切干净的。'},
{q:'Why do you rinse a coffee filter before you use it?',
  ez:'“That is equilibration. It is the first of the four chromatography steps. You put the stationary phase into the right condition. It is the condition the separation assumes. So nothing from the resin ends up in your sample. And the sample meets the buffer it is supposed to meet. A column that has not been equilibrated will not bind reproducibly.”',
  ezcn:'<b>那就是「平衡」——层析四步里的第一步。</b><b>你是在把固定相调到分离所假定的那个条件上</b>：<b>这样树脂本身的东西不会跑进你的样品，而样品遇到的也正是它该遇到的缓冲液</b>。<b>没平衡过的柱子，结合就不可重复。</b>',
 mean:'<b>便装问题。</b>他问的是<b>平衡</b>那一步——四步里最容易被跳过去的一步。',
 say:'“That is equilibration, the first of the four chromatography steps. You are putting the stationary phase into the condition the separation assumes, so that nothing from the resin itself ends up in your sample and so that the sample meets the buffer it is supposed to meet. A column that has not been equilibrated will not bind reproducibly.”',
 tail:'四步里她最容易漏掉的就是第一步，因为它「什么都没发生」。<b>漏掉它，后面三步的条件就没有定义。</b>',
 odd:1},
{q:'You have a bucket of sand with iron filings in it. How do you get the filings out?',
  ez:'“That is batch chromatography with magnetic beads. It has the same four steps. You mix the binder through the whole sample. You do not pack a column. Then you pull the beads out with a magnet. You do not flow buffer past them. Batch format suits some resins. It suits those with low dynamic binding capacity. It also suits high throughput work and robotics.”',
  ezcn:'<b>那是用磁珠做的批式层析，四步一样。</b><b>你把结合剂直接混进整个样品里，而不是装一根柱子；然后用磁铁把珠子吸出来，而不是让缓冲液流过它们。</b><b>批式格式适合动态载量低的树脂，也适合高通量和机器人操作。</b>',
 mean:'<b>便装问题。</b>这是<b>批式层析加磁珠</b>，而且整个四步框架都在里面。',
 say:'“That is batch chromatography with magnetic beads, and it has the same four steps. You mix the binder through the whole sample instead of packing a column, then you pull the beads out with a magnet instead of flowing buffer past them. Batch format suits resins with low dynamic binding capacity, and it suits high throughput work and robotics.”',
 tail:'柱式换分辨率，批式换通量和容量。<b>两者的四步是一样的，回收方式不一样。</b>',
 odd:1},
{q:'Your key is stuck in a lock. Do you pull harder, or do you find a different key?',
  ez:'“Those are three different operations. And they are the ones I must keep apart on a column. Competing something off with a better binder is elution. Imidazole on a nickel column is exactly that. Forcing it with acid or a chelator is destruction. The chelator takes the nickel with it. Cutting the tag off with a protease is a third thing. It is not elution at all.”',
  ezcn:'<b>那是三个不同的操作，而这三个正是我在柱子上必须分清楚的。</b><b>用一个更强的结合剂把它竞争下来 ＝ 洗脱</b>（<b>镍柱上的咪唑就是</b>）。<b>用酸或螯合剂硬来 ＝ 破坏</b>（<b>螯合剂会把镍一起带走</b>）。<b>用蛋白酶把标签切掉 ＝ 第三件事，它根本不是洗脱。</b>',
 mean:'<b>便装问题，而且它就是三层那件事。</b>用力 ＝ 破坏，换钥匙 ＝ 竞争，拆门 ＝ 切除。',
 say:'“Those are three different operations and they are the ones I have to keep apart on a column. Competing something off with a better binder is elution, and imidazole on a nickel column is exactly that. Forcing it with acid or with a chelator is destruction, and the chelator takes the nickel with it. Cutting the tag off the protein with a protease is a third thing, and it is not how you get the protein off the resin at all.”',
 tail:'<b>这一条是整张卡的寓言版本。</b>被问蒙的时候回到这里：他问的是竞争、破坏，还是切割？',
 odd:1},
{q:'Why does washing powder get grease off a plate when water alone will not?',
  ez:'“A detergent has two ends. One end is nonpolar. The other end is charged. So it can sit between grease and water. It then carries the grease away. S D S does the same to a protein on a gel. It unfolds the protein. It coats it with a uniform negative charge. That is about one molecule per two residues. And it makes the protein rod shaped. Those three things are why migration depends on molecular weight.”',
  ezcn:'<b>去污剂有两头：一头非极性，一头带电</b>——<b>所以它能夹在油脂和水之间，把油脂带走</b>。<b>SDS 对胶上的蛋白干的是同一件事：把蛋白摊开、按每两个残基约一个分子的比例给它裹上均匀的负电荷、并把它变成棒状。</b><b>正是这三件事一起，让迁移率只取决于分子量。</b>',
 mean:'<b>便装问题。</b>去污剂就是 SDS，而 SDS 在这张卡上出现了两次：一次在反相的变性条件旁边，一次在 SDS-PAGE 里。',
 say:'“A detergent has a nonpolar end and a charged end, so it can sit between grease and water and carry the grease away. That is also what SDS does to a protein on a gel. It unfolds the protein, it coats it with a uniform negative charge at about one molecule per two residues, and it makes it rod-shaped. Those three things together are why migration then depends on molecular weight alone.”',
 tail:'同一个分子，在盘子上叫去污，在胶上叫变性。<b>疏水效应那一格在卡 <b>x-bonds</b>。</b>',
 odd:1}
],

ask:[
 {g:'⚠ 你凭什么说纯化成功了', gn:'⚠ <b>2026-09-23 审查补的，这一条是这张卡最该有而原来没有的。</b>卡上层析有 26 处、SDS-PAGE 有 23 处，<b>但 <code>specific activity</code>／<code>yield</code>／<code>fold purification</code> 一共只有 4 处</b> —— <b>也就是说，「怎么证明」那一半是空的</b>。<b>纯化题最标准的追问就是这一句。</b>', items:[
{r:'高', q:'How do you show that a purification actually worked?',
    ez:'“A gel alone cannot answer this. A gel shows purity. It does not show whether the protein still works. It does not show how much I lost. So I show a purification table. The key number is specific activity. It is units of activity per milligram of total protein. Purification lowers the denominator and tries not to touch the numerator. So a rising specific activity means contaminants are gone. The table has one row per step. Each row gives total protein, total activity and specific activity. Two derived numbers follow. Yield is the activity left as a percentage of the start. Purification fold is the specific activity divided by the starting one. Every step is a trade. Specific activity goes up and some total activity is always lost. A good purification raises specific activity a lot and loses as little activity as possible.”',
    ezcn:'⚠ <b>先把结论说出口：单跑胶答不了这个问题。</b><b>胶看得见纯度，看不见蛋白还活不活、也看不见我丢了多少 —— 一条漂亮的单带也可能是一管死蛋白。</b><b>所以我拿<b>纯化表</b>说话。</b><b>核心的那个数是<b>比活</b>：每毫克总蛋白的酶活力单位。</b><b>纯化干的事就是把分母往下拿、尽量别动分子 —— 所以比活上升就等于杂蛋白被拿掉了。</b><b>表上<b>一步一行</b>，每行给<b>总蛋白</b>、<b>总活力</b>、<b>比活</b>；再由它们算出两个数：<b>得率</b>＝剩下的活力占起始的百分比，<b>纯化倍数</b>＝这一步的比活除以起始比活。</b>⚠ <b>为什么非要两个数：因为每一步都是一场交易 —— 比活涨上去，总活力一定掉一些。好的纯化是比活涨得多、活力丢得少。只报一个数是在藏事。</b>',
 en:'“I show a purification table. The key number is specific activity, which is units of enzyme activity per milligram of total protein. The table has one row per step, and each row gives total protein, total activity and specific activity. Two derived numbers follow. Yield is the activity remaining as a percentage of the start, and purification fold is the specific activity divided by the starting value. A good purification raises specific activity a lot while losing as little activity as possible, and those two pull against each other, so the table is what shows the trade. A gel alone cannot show it, because a gel says the contaminating bands are gone but says nothing about whether the target is still active. This is general knowledge.”',
 cn:'⚠ <b>整条 general</b>：<code>specifická aktivita</code> 全书 0 命中。<br><br>⚠ <b>这是这张卡上最大的一个洞</b>，而且是她自己的地盘：<b>卡上把「怎么做」讲透了（层析 26 处、SDS-PAGE 23 处），「怎么证明」却几乎没有。</b><br><br><b>他接着最可能问两句</b>：<br>① <b>「一个活力单位是什么？」</b> —— 在规定条件下每分钟转化 1 µmol 底物所需的酶量。<b>（这一条卡 18 的「催化效率」那一组里有 molecular activity／turnover number，可以接过去。）</b><br>② <b>「得率为什么会掉？」</b> —— 每一步都会丢：柱子上不回收的、变性的、被蛋白酶切的。<b>敢说「我这一步得率 60%」比说「很高」有说服力得多。</b>'},
 ]},
{g:'定义类', gn:'这张卡自己用到的词，他会一个一个拎出来问。<b>卡欠这些解释，所以每一个都要在这里给出来。</b>', items:[
  {r:'高', q:'What is FPLC, and how is it different from HPLC?',
    ez:'“F P L C is the instrument, not a separation principle. It stands for fast protein liquid chromatography. It is a pump, a column, a U V detector and a fraction collector. The pump runs a programmed gradient. The detector watches absorbance at two hundred eighty nanometres. The collector cuts the eluate into fractions. The column decides the principle. Put an ion exchange column on it and you separate by charge. Put a size exclusion column on it and you separate by size. Put an affinity column on it and you separate by a specific interaction. H P L C runs at much higher pressure with small rigid particles. That suits small molecules. F P L C keeps the pressure low and the buffers aqueous, so the protein stays folded.”',
    ezcn:'<b>FPLC 是一台仪器，不是一种分离原理。</b><b>全称是快速蛋白液相层析。</b><b>它就是泵 ＋ 柱子 ＋ 紫外检测器 ＋ 收集器</b>：<b>泵跑一个编好的梯度，检测器盯 280 纳米的吸收，收集器把流出液切成一管管。</b><b>原理是柱子决定的</b>：<b>换离子交换柱就按电荷分，换分子排阻柱就按大小分，换亲和柱就按特异相互作用分。</b><b>HPLC 压力高得多、填料小而硬，适合小分子；FPLC 压力低、缓冲液是水相，所以蛋白能保持折叠。</b>',
   en:'“FPLC is the instrument rather than a separation principle. It stands for fast protein liquid chromatography, and it is a pump, a column, a UV detector and a fraction collector. The pump runs a programmed gradient, the detector watches absorbance at 280 nanometres, and the collector cuts the eluate into fractions. The principle is decided by the column: an ion-exchange column separates by charge, a size-exclusion column by size, an affinity column by a specific interaction. HPLC runs at much higher pressure with small rigid particles. That suits small molecules. FPLC keeps the pressure low and the buffers aqueous, so the protein stays folded.”',
   cn:'⚠ <b>她 2026-09-25 说怕被问这个。</b>查过：<b>「FPLC」这个词全套卡上一次都没出现，但内容全在这张卡</b>（离子交换、分子排阻、亲和、梯度洗脱、A280）—— <b>缺的只是这个名字。</b><br><b>判据一句：FPLC 是仪器，柱子才是原理。</b>他问「你用 FPLC 做什么」，你就说你装的是哪根柱子、按什么分。<br><b>跟 HPLC 的区别答两点就够</b>：<b>压力</b>和<b>为了让蛋白别变性</b>。<span class="pg">通用</span>'},

{r:'高', q:'What is chromatography?',
    ez:'“It is a process for separating the components of a mixture. A mobile phase flows through a stationary phase. The stationary phase is fixed and porous. The components travel at different speeds. The speed depends on how much each interacts with the stationary phase. In this context the aim is enrichment. I want to isolate the target from contaminating cellular species.”',
    ezcn:'<b>层析 ＝ 分离混合物各组分的一种方法</b>：<b>流动相流过固定的、多孔的固定相</b>，<b>各组分按「跟固定相作用多强」走出不同的速度</b>。<b>在这个语境里目的很具体：把目标蛋白从细胞里那些杂质中富集或分离出来。</b>',
 en:'“A process for separating the components of a mixture. A mobile phase flows through a fixed porous stationary phase, and the components travel at different speeds depending on how much they interact with the stationary phase. In this context the aim is to enrich or isolate the target from contaminating cellular species.”',
 cn:'定义 ＋ 两相 ＋ 目的，三件一句话给完。<span class="pg">L4 s.8–10</span> <b>先说它是什么，再说判据</b>——这是全套卡的通例。'},
{r:'中', q:'What is a column volume, and why is everything measured in them?',
  ez:'“A column volume is the volume of the packed bed. Wash and elution steps are counted in them. Typically each step is about ten column volumes. The reason is transferability. A protocol written in column volumes moves between sizes. It works on a one millilitre column. It also works on a hundred millilitre one. Millilitres would not transfer that way.”',
  ezcn:'<b>柱体积 ＝ 填料床的体积。</b><b>洗涤和洗脱都按柱体积计数，通常各约 10 个柱体积。</b><b>为什么用柱体积而不是毫升：这样写出来的方案可以在不同尺寸之间搬——1 mL 的柱子和 100 mL 的柱子用同一份方案；写毫升就搬不过去。</b>',
 en:'“A column volume is the volume of the packed bed. Wash and elution steps are counted in column volumes, typically about 10 of each. Using column volumes rather than millilitres makes a protocol transferable between a 1 millilitre column and a 100 millilitre one.”',
 cn:'「为什么用柱体积而不是毫升」这一条<b>笔记没有说</b>，是通用的实验室常识。数字（各约 10 CV）在幻灯片上。<span class="pg">L4 s.8–10</span>'},
{r:'中', q:'What is binding capacity, and what is dynamic binding capacity?',
  ez:'“Binding capacity is how much target one millilitre of resin can hold. It is measured in milligrams. It runs from about half a milligram to two hundred. Dynamic binding capacity is the same thing under flow. It is not measured at equilibrium. So it depends on the association rate constant. The resin must grab the protein as it goes past. Glutathione Sepharose is noted for a low dynamic capacity.”',
  ezcn:'<b>结合容量 ＝ 每毫升填料能装多少毫克目标蛋白，大约从 0.5 到 200 mg/mL。</b><b>动态结合容量 ＝ 同一件事但在流动条件下测的，不是在平衡下测的——所以它取决于结合速率常数：填料必须在蛋白流过去的那一瞬间抓住它。</b><b>谷胱甘肽琼脂糖就是被特别点名「动态容量低」的那一个。</b>',
 en:'“Binding capacity is how many milligrams of target one millilitre of resin can hold, and it runs from about 0.5 to 200. Dynamic binding capacity is the capacity measured under flow rather than at equilibrium, so it depends on the association rate constant. Glutathione Sepharose is specifically noted as having a low dynamic capacity.”',
 cn:'<b>这一条直接接到卡 <b>02</b></b>：动态容量依赖 k<sub>on</sub>，而 k<sub>on</sub> 正是 Kd 的分母。<b>结合得慢的树脂，在流动条件下表现比它的静态数字差。</b><span class="pg">L4 s.11–12</span>'},
{r:'中', q:'What is a chelator?',
  ez:'“A chelator is a molecule that binds a metal ion at several points at once. So it holds that ion very tightly. E D T A is the common one. It is fatal to an immobilised metal affinity resin. That resin works only by keeping its metal ions. A chelator takes them away.”',
  ezcn:'<b>螯合剂 ＝ 一个同时从好几个位点结合金属离子、因而抓得非常牢的分子。</b><b>常见的是 EDTA。</b>⚠ <b>它对固定化金属亲和填料是致命的：那种填料全靠留住自己的金属离子工作，而螯合剂正好把金属拿走。</b>',
 en:'“A molecule that binds a metal ion at several points at once and therefore holds it very tightly. EDTA is the common one. It is fatal to an immobilised metal affinity resin, because that resin works only by keeping its metal ions.”',
 cn:'这个词<b>承重</b>：不懂它，「EDTA 毁柱子」这句话就只是一条要背的禁令。<b>NTA 本身也是一个螯合基团</b>——同一个化学，一个把镍抓在树脂上，一个把镍抢走。<span class="pg">L4 s.11–12</span>'},
{r:'中', q:'What is an isoelectric point?',
  ez:'“The isoelectric point is a p H value. At that p H the protein carries no net charge. Above it the protein is negative. Below it the protein is positive. There are two ways to get it. You can measure it by isoelectric focusing. Or you can calculate it from the sequence. Expasy Prot Param does that calculation.”',
  ezcn:'<b>等电点 ＝ 蛋白净电荷为零的那个 pH。</b><b>高于它，蛋白带负电；低于它，带正电。</b><b>两种拿到它的办法：用等电聚焦测出来，或者用 Expasy ProtParam 从序列算出来。</b>',
 en:'“The pH at which a protein carries no net charge. Above it the protein is negative and below it the protein is positive. You can measure it by isoelectric focusing, or calculate it from the sequence with Expasy ProtParam.”',
 cn:'pH 本身和它为什么是对数尺度，整张在卡 <b>x-ph</b>；带电侧链 Arg、Lys、Asp、Glu 在卡 <b>aa</b>。<span class="pg">L4 s.14–15</span>'},
{r:'中', q:'What is a coordination bond?',
  ez:'“A coordination bond is formed by donating a lone electron pair. The pair is donated to a metal ion. It matters here for one reason. It does not depend on the protein being folded. So it survives denaturants. Every other affinity interaction is destroyed by them.”',
  ezcn:'<b>配位键 ＝ 把一对孤对电子给到一个金属离子上而形成的键。</b><b>它在这里之所以要紧，只有一个理由：它不依赖蛋白是否折叠，所以它扛得住变性剂——而其他所有的亲和相互作用都会被变性剂毁掉。</b>',
 en:'“A bond formed by donating a lone electron pair to a metal ion. It matters here because it does not depend on the protein being folded, so it survives denaturants that destroy every other affinity interaction.”',
 cn:'⚠ <b>停在这里。</b>再往下就是哪个空轨道、八面体、d⁸，那是配位场理论，不是生化（LOGIC 第 5 条的内容闸门）。各种键的分类在卡 <b>x-bonds</b>。'},
{r:'中', q:'What does native mean when you say a native N-terminus?',
  ez:'“A native N terminus is one carrying no leftover residues. Nothing is left over from the cleavage site. Most proteases recognise a linear sequence. They cut inside that sequence. So whatever lies downstream of the cut stays attached. Only S U M O protease avoids that. It recognises a fold rather than a sequence.”',
  ezcn:'<b>天然 N 端 ＝ 上面没有任何从切割位点残留下来的残基。</b><b>大多数蛋白酶识别的是一段线性序列，而且是在这段序列内部切开，所以切口下游的那些残基就留在你的蛋白上了。</b><b>唯一避开这件事的是 SUMO 蛋白酶——它识别的是一个折叠结构，不是一段序列。</b>',
 en:'“It means an N-terminus carrying no residues left over from a cleavage site. Most proteases recognise a linear sequence and cut inside it, so whatever lies downstream of the cut stays attached. Only SUMO protease avoids that, because it recognises a fold rather than a sequence.”',
 cn:'<b>「native」在这句话里跟「native fold」不是一个意思</b>，指的是序列上没有多余残基。这两个 native 在同一张卡上出现过，值得自己先分清。<span class="pg">L5 s.8</span>'},
  {r:'高', q:'How do you regenerate a nickel affinity column, and what must never touch it?',
    ez:'“The nickel is held by the chelating groups on the resin, so regenerating it means stripping the metal and putting it back. I wash the column with E D T A. That pulls the nickel off. Then I wash out the E D T A. Then I recharge the resin with fresh nickel sulphate. Then I equilibrate. What must never touch it is E D T A in a sample, because that strips the column mid run. Strong reducing agents are the other one. High D T T reduces the nickel and it precipitates, so for a His purification I keep the reducing agent low, or use T C E P or a little beta mercaptoethanol instead.”',
    ezcn:'<b>镂是被树脂上的螬合基团握着的，所以再生就是把金属剥下来、再上回去。</b><b>用 EDTA 洗柱子把镂拉走，洗掉 EDTA，再用新的硫酸镂给树脂充上，然后平衡。</b>⚠ <b>绝对不能碰的是样品里的 EDTA —— 那会在上样中途把柱子剥掉。</b><b>另一个是强还原剂：高浓度 DTT 会把镂还原掉、析出来，所以做 His 纯化时还原剂要低，或者换成 TCEP、或少量 β-巇基乙醇。</b>',
   en:'“The nickel is held by chelating groups on the resin, so regenerating it means stripping the metal and putting it back. I wash the column with EDTA, and that pulls the nickel off. Then I wash out the EDTA. Then I recharge the resin with fresh nickel sulphate and equilibrate. What must never touch it is EDTA in a sample, because that strips the column mid-run. Strong reducing agents are the other one: high DTT reduces the nickel and it precipitates, so for a His purification I keep the reducing agent low, or use TCEP or a little beta-mercaptoethanol instead.”',
   cn:'⚠ <b>2026-09-25 补的，全套卡 0 命中</b>。<b>两个禁忌都要说：EDTA 和 高 DTT。</b><br><b>因为它们背后是同一个道理：螬合是一个平衡，可逆。</b>接本卡 His 标签与呸唑洗脱那一格，以及 Hudeček 名下 TCEP 那一条。<span class="pg">通用</span>'},
  {r:'高', q:'What does SDS-PAGE actually separate by, and why does SDS make that work?',
    ez:'“By size, and only because S D S removes everything else. S D S is an anionic detergent. It unfolds the protein and coats it, so every chain carries roughly the same charge per unit length. Native charge and native shape stop mattering. A reducing agent breaks the disulfides so subunits run separately. Then the gel is a sieve, and mobility depends on chain length. Two things to watch. Glycosylated proteins and very acidic proteins run at the wrong apparent mass. And a gradient or a stacking gel is what makes the bands sharp, because it concentrates everything into a thin start line first.”',
    ezcn:'<b>按大小分，而且只因为 SDS 把其余变量都拿掉了。</b><b>SDS 是阴离子表面活性剂：它把蛋白展开并裹上，于是每条链单位长度带的电荷差不多 —— 天然电荷和天然形状就不重要了。</b><b>还原剂把二硫键断掉，亚基就各跑各的。</b><b>然后胶就是个筛子，迁移只看链长。</b>⚠ <b>两件要盯的：糖基化的蛋白和强酸性蛋白会跑出错的表观分子量；以及浓缩胶（或浓度梯度）才是条带清晰的原因 —— 它先把东西挤成一条细线再开跑。</b>',
   en:'“By size, and only because SDS removes everything else. SDS is an anionic detergent: it unfolds the protein and coats it, so every chain carries roughly the same charge per unit length and native charge and shape stop mattering. A reducing agent breaks the disulfides so subunits run separately. The gel is then a sieve and mobility depends on chain length. Two things to watch. Glycosylated proteins and very acidic proteins run at the wrong apparent mass. And a stacking gel is what makes the bands sharp. It concentrates everything into a thin start line first.”',
   cn:'⚠ <b>SDS-PAGE 在卡上只被提到过，没有任何一格正面讲。</b>2026-09-25 补。<br><b>判据一句：它不是「按大小分」那么简单，是「SDS 把电荷和形状这两个变量消掉了，所以才只剩大小」。</b><br><b>接卡 01</b>（二硫键与四级结构）、<b>13</b>（糖基化）、本卡的纯度检查。<span class="pg">通用</span>'},
]},

{g:'⚠ 三层分开问', gn:'<b>这一组是这张卡的核心。</b>三个问题听起来几乎一样，而且他可以随便问哪一个。<b>每答一句之前先默认一次：他问的是哪一层。</b>', items:[
{r:'实测', q:'How would you neutralise the effect of a histidine tag?',
    ez:'“By competing it off the resin with imidazole. The tag binds for one reason. The histidine side chain is an imidazole ring. That ring coordinates a nickel ion. Free imidazole is the bare version of that side chain. So adding it displaces the tag. Elution uses two hundred and fifty to five hundred millimolar. The wash already contains twenty to forty.”',
    ezcn:'用<b>咪唑</b>把它从柱子上<b>竞争下来</b>。标签能挂住只有一个理由：<b>组氨酸的侧链就是一个咪唑环</b>，它配位镍离子。<b>游离咪唑就是那个侧链的光杆版</b>，加进去就把标签顶下来了。洗脱用 <b>250–500 mM</b>，洗涤液里本来就有 <b>20–40 mM</b>。',
 en:'“By competing it off the resin with imidazole. The tag binds because the histidine side chain is an imidazole ring coordinating a nickel ion. Free imidazole is the bare version of that side chain, so adding it displaces the tag. Elution uses 250 to 500 millimolar, and the wash already contains 20 to 40.”',
 cn:'<b>2026-09-01 实测，丢分最重的一处。</b>他问的是洗脱层，答成了移除层（protease）。<b>两个答案都对，但后一个不回答被问的那个问题。</b>整条推理在 LOGIC 第 9 条。<br><b>触发词</b>：neutralise · elute · release · get it off the column · recover it from the resin ——<b>全部是同一层</b>。',
 warn:'⚠ 如果一时分不清他问的是哪一层，<b>就把分层本身说出来</b>：“Do you mean getting it off the resin, or removing the tag from the protein? Those are different operations.” <b>反问一句不丢分，答错一层才丢分。</b>'},
{r:'高', q:'So how do you remove the tag?',
    ez:'“With a protease. And that is a separate operation from elution. T E V recognises the sequence E N L Y F Q. It cuts before glycine or serine. PreScission recognises L E V L F Q. It cuts before glycine proline. You remove a tag for one reason. It interferes with the experiment you are about to do. You do not remove it to get the protein off the column.”',
    ezcn:'<b>用蛋白酶切，而且这跟「洗脱」是两码事。</b><b>TEV 识别 ENLYFQ，在甘氨酸或丝氨酸前面切；PreScission 识别 LEVLFQ，在甘氨酸-脯氨酸前面切。</b>⚠ <b>去标签的理由只有一个：它会干扰你接下来要做的实验</b>——<b>不是为了把蛋白从柱子上弄下来。</b>',
 en:'“With a protease, and that is a separate operation from elution. TEV recognises ENLYFQ and cuts before glycine or serine. PreScission recognises LEVLFQ and cuts before glycine proline. You remove a tag because it interferes with the experiment you are about to do, not because you want the protein off the column.”',
 cn:'<b>开头那半句「and that is a separate operation from elution」是故意的</b>——它向他表明你知道刚才那一题和这一题不是同一题。<span class="pg">L5 s.8</span>',
 good:'加分：切完还要<b>把酶弄走</b>。用带 His 标签的蛋白酶，整管再过一次镍柱——酶和没切干净的融合蛋白都留在柱上，目标从穿透液出来。这叫<b>反向镍柱</b>。'},
{r:'高', q:'Does EDTA elute a His-tagged protein?',
    ez:'“It takes the protein off. But it is not elution. E D T A is a chelator. So it strips the nickel ions off the resin. And the column is then finished. E D T A is also a routine lysis buffer component. It is added to inhibit metal dependent proteases. So this is a real hazard rather than a method. Reducing agents do the same damage by another route.”',
    ezcn:'<b>它确实能把蛋白弄下来，但那不是洗脱。</b><b>EDTA 是螯合剂，它把镍离子从树脂上剥走——那根柱子就废了。</b>⚠ <b>而 EDTA 又是裂解缓冲液的常规成分（加它是为了抑制金属依赖的蛋白酶）</b>，<b>所以这是一个真实的事故，不是一种方法</b>。<b>还原剂走另一条路造成同样的破坏。</b>',
 en:'“It takes the protein off, but it is not elution. EDTA is a chelator, so it strips the nickel ions off the resin and the column is finished. And EDTA is a routine lysis buffer component, added to inhibit metal-dependent proteases, so this is a real hazard rather than a method. Reducing agents do the same damage by another route.”',
 cn:'⚠ <b>这是一道分层陷阱题</b>：它长得像洗脱层的问题，答案其实在「破坏」那一层。<b>回答里必须出现「takes the protein off but is not elution」这个转折</b>，否则听上去像你以为 EDTA 是个选项。<span class="pg">L4 s.11–12</span>',
 warn:'⚠ 但<b>同一个 EDTA 在 FLAG 柱上就是正确的洗脱剂</b>，因为 M1 单抗的结合依赖钙离子。<b>他要是接着问这个，别硬撑「EDTA 总是有害的」</b>——答：“On a FLAG column EDTA is the eluent, because that binding is calcium-dependent. On a nickel column it destroys the resin. The reagent does not have a meaning on its own.”'},
{r:'高', q:'Why does the wash contain imidazole? Has elution not already started?',
    ez:'“It has, in a sense. And that is the point. Washing and eluting differ only in concentration. Twenty to forty millimolar displaces host proteins. Those proteins carry a few surface histidines by accident. A real run of six histidines holds on at that concentration. Then two hundred and fifty to five hundred takes the tag off as well.”',
    ezcn:'<b>某种意义上确实已经开始了，而这正是要点：洗涤和洗脱的差别只在浓度上。</b><b>20–40 mM 把那些「碰巧表面带几个组氨酸」的宿主蛋白顶下来，而真正的六聚组氨酸在这个浓度下还挂得住</b>；<b>然后 250–500 mM 把标签也一起带下来。</b>',
 en:'“It has, in a sense, and that is the point. Washing and eluting differ only in concentration. 20 to 40 millimolar displaces host proteins that carry a few surface histidines by accident, and a real run of six histidines holds on at that concentration. Then 250 to 500 takes the tag off as well.”',
 cn:'<b>承认「在某种意义上是的」比否认强</b>，因为它承认了洗涤和洗脱是同一条连续曲线。数学版本在段 4 的推导里：<code>K<sub>d</sub>′ = K<sub>d</sub>(1+[I]/K<sub>I</sub>)</code>，你一直在挪同一个数。'},
{r:'中', q:'Cutting the tag off gives you the original protein back, does it not?',
  ez:'“Not exactly. A sequence recognising protease cuts inside a linear motif. So the residues downstream of the cut stay on the protein. After T E V your protein permanently starts with an extra glycine. S U M O protease is the exception. It recognises the three dimensional fold of the S U M O domain. And it cuts exactly at the C terminus of that domain.”',
  ezcn:'<b>不完全是。</b><b>识别序列的蛋白酶是在一段线性基序内部切开的，所以切口下游的残基会永久留在你的蛋白上——用 TEV 之后，你的蛋白开头就永远多一个甘氨酸。</b><b>例外是 SUMO 蛋白酶：它识别的是 SUMO 结构域的三维折叠，正好切在那个结构域的 C 端。</b><b>什么时候非要天然 N 端：N 端序列本身有功能（信号肽、N 端规则、后续偶联），或者做结构生物学、不想要多余的柔性残基。</b>',
 en:'“Not exactly. A sequence-recognising protease cuts inside a linear motif, so the residues downstream of the cut stay on the protein. After TEV your protein permanently starts with an extra glycine. SUMO protease is the exception, because it recognises the three-dimensional fold of the SUMO domain and cuts exactly at its C-terminus.”',
 cn:'⚠ <b>这是移除层内部的陷阱。</b>说「切掉就还原了」是错的。笔记把这一条标了 beyond the slides，幻灯片上只写了 SUMO 蛋白酶「给出天然 N 端、特异性 100%」。<span class="pg">L5 s.8</span>',
 good:'什么时候非要天然 N 端不可：N 端序列本身有功能（信号肽、N 端规则、后续偶联），以及做结构生物学、不想要多余的柔性残基。'},
{r:'中', q:'Streptavidin and biotin bind tightest, so why not always use that?',
  ez:'“Because the strength is the advantage and the liability at once. The dissociation constant is ten to the minus fifteen molar. So you can wash under very harsh conditions. And you lose nothing. But you also cannot get the protein off again. Not under native conditions. So there are two ways round it. You engineer the affinity down. Or you do not elute at all and work on the beads.”',
  ezcn:'因为<b>那个强度同时是优点和负担</b>。<b>解离常数是 10⁻¹⁵ M，所以你可以用很苛刻的条件洗而一点都不丢；可你也就没法在天然条件下把蛋白弄下来了。</b><b>两条出路：把亲和力工程改低（Streptactin 配脱硫生物素就是这么做的），或者干脆不洗脱、直接在珠子上做实验。</b>',
 en:'“Because the strength is the advantage and the liability at the same time. The dissociation constant is 10 to the minus 15 molar, so you can wash under very harsh conditions and lose nothing. But you also cannot get the protein off again under native conditions. So either you engineer the affinity down, and Streptactin with desthiobiotin is exactly that, or you do not elute at all and work on the beads.”',
 cn:'⚠ <b>这一题的错误形状跟「中和 His 标签」是同一个</b>：只答了结合层，把洗脱层丢了。<b>凡是「哪个最强」的问题，答完结合层必须立刻接洗脱层。</b><span class="pg">L4 s.23</span>'}
]},

{g:'他要数字怎么办', gn:'<b>先分清他问的是「具体量」还是「类别边界」。</b>前者报数（这张卡的数全在笔记里），后者给判据加反例，<b>绝不编</b>。LOGIC 第 11 条。', items:[
{r:'高', q:'How much imidazole exactly?',
    ez:'“Twenty to forty millimolar in the wash. Two hundred and fifty to five hundred in the elution. Those are working ranges rather than single values. The right number depends on two things. It depends on how many histidines the tag has. And on how much the particular host background binds. In practice you find it by running a small gradient once.”',
    ezcn:'<b>洗涤 20–40 mM，洗脱 250–500 mM。</b><b>这些是工作范围不是单一数值</b>：<b>正确的数字取决于标签有几个组氨酸，以及这个宿主的本底结合有多强</b>。<b>实操上就是先跑一次小梯度把它找出来。</b>',
 en:'“20 to 40 millimolar in the wash and 250 to 500 in the elution. Those are working ranges rather than a single value, because the right number depends on how many histidines the tag has and on how much the particular host background binds. In practice you find it by running a small gradient once.”',
 cn:'<b>这是「具体量」，要报数。</b>两个范围都在幻灯片上。<span class="pg">L4 s.20</span> 「跑个小梯度试出来」这一句<b>是通用做法，笔记里没有</b>。'},
{r:'高', q:'How far from the pI do you work?',
    ez:'“About one p H unit away. Too close to the p I and the net charge is too small. Then binding is weak. Too far and contaminating proteins pick up charge too. Then they bind as well. So it is a window rather than a threshold.”',
    ezcn:'<b>大约离等电点一个 pH 单位。</b><b>离 pI 太近，净电荷太小，结合就弱；离得太远，杂蛋白也带上足够电荷，一起挂上来了。</b><b>所以它是一个窗口，不是一个阈值。</b>',
 en:'“About one pH unit. Too close to the pI and the net charge is too small, so binding is weak. Too far and contaminating proteins pick up enough charge to bind as well. So it is a window rather than a threshold.”',
 cn:'一个 pH 单位这个数在笔记里，<b>但标的是 beyond the slides</b>，被追问出处要说清。<b>而且这是个窗口不是门槛</b>——两边各有一个失败模式，把两个都说出来比报一个数稳。'},
{r:'中', q:'How pure is a protein after one nickel column?',
  ez:'“That is not a number the method has. It depends on three things. It depends on how much host background carries surface histidines. It depends on how stringent the wash was. And it depends on how much you loaded. That is relative to the capacity. What I can give you is the diagnostic. A large elution peak with many contaminant bands means one thing. The wash was not stringent enough.”',
  ezcn:'⚠ <b>这个方法本身给不出一个数。</b><b>它取决于三件事：宿主背景里有多少蛋白表面带组氨酸 · 洗得多严格 · 上样量相对于容量是多少。</b><b>我能给的是判断依据：洗脱峰很大、杂带很多，说明洗涤不够严格。</b>',
 en:'“That is not a number the method has. It depends on how much of the host background carries surface histidines, on how stringent the wash was, and on how much you loaded relative to the capacity. What I can give you is the diagnostic. A large elution peak with many contaminant bands means the wash was not stringent enough.”',
 cn:'⚠ <b>这是「类别边界」型的问题，没有数，也不该有。</b>给判据，给一个能看见的判据（胶上的带），<b>不要编一个百分数</b>。诊断那一条笔记标了 beyond the slides。<span class="pg">L4 s.8–10</span>'},
{r:'中', q:'How much can you load onto a size exclusion column?',
  ez:'“Under five per cent of the column volume. Above that the peaks broaden. And the resolution collapses. That is a hard limit. It is also the reason for something else. Size exclusion can never be the first step.”',
  ezcn:'<b>不超过柱体积的 5%。</b><b>超过之后峰会变宽，分辨率就垮了。</b><b>这是一条硬限制，而且它正是「凝胶过滤永远不能当第一步」的原因。</b>',
 en:'“Under 5 per cent of the column volume. Above that the peaks broaden and the resolution collapses. That is a hard limit, and it is the reason size exclusion can never be the first step.”',
 cn:'<b>这是这张卡上最该报的一个数</b>，因为整个三段顺序就是被它逼出来的。<span class="pg">L5 s.5–7 · L5 s.9</span>'},
{r:'中', q:'How sensitive is a Coomassie gel?',
  ez:'“About fifty to a hundred nanograms per band. Silver detects about one to five. So silver is ten to fifty times more sensitive. But silver quantifies poorly. And the procedure is laborious. So Coomassie stays the default. You switch only when chasing trace contaminants.”',
  ezcn:'<b>每条带大约 50–100 ng。</b><b>银染能到 1–5 ng，也就是灵敏 10–50 倍；但银染定量很差、操作又繁琐，所以考马斯仍然是默认选择——只有在追痕量杂质时才换。</b>',
 en:'“About 50 to 100 nanograms per band. Silver detects about 1 to 5, so it is 10 to 50 times more sensitive, but it quantifies poorly and the procedure is laborious. So Coomassie stays the default unless you are chasing trace contaminants.”',
 cn:'数字在笔记里。<b>这一条直接走到停止句</b>：「纯」是一句关于检测限的话，不是关于样品的话。'}
]},

{g:'排序和判断', gn:'这一组问的都是<b>「为什么是这个顺序」</b>。答判据，不要答清单。', items:[
{r:'高', q:'How would you design a purification from scratch?',
    ez:'“In three stages. Capture, intermediate purification, polishing. Capture is a high capacity specific method. It is taken straight from crude lysate. Usually that is affinity. The volume is large there. What you need is capacity. Intermediate purification is ion exchange. Or hydrophobic interaction. By then the volume is small enough. So resolution is worth chasing. Polishing is size exclusion. It also sets the final storage buffer.”',
    ezcn:'<b>三段：捕获 → 中度纯化 → 精修。</b><b>捕获</b>：<b>直接从粗裂解液上样，用高载量的专一方法（通常是亲和）</b>——<b>那一步体积大，要的是载量</b>。<b>中度纯化</b>：<b>离子交换或疏水作用，此时体积已经小到值得追求分辨率</b>。<b>精修</b>：<b>分子筛，同时顺便把最终的保存缓冲液换好。</b>',
 en:'“Capture, intermediate purification, polishing. Capture is a high-capacity specific method taken straight from crude lysate, usually affinity, because the volume is large and what you need is capacity. Intermediate purification is ion exchange or hydrophobic interaction, once the volume is small enough that resolution is worth chasing. Polishing is size exclusion, which also sets the final storage buffer.”',
 cn:'四个选择标准（幻灯片上）：<b>产率、分辨率、通量、时间</b>。产率那一栏：高是 IEX、Ni-NTA、疏水、protein A/G；中是 Streptactin、直链淀粉；低是 SEC 和 FLAG。<span class="pg">L5 s.9</span>'},
{r:'高', q:'Why not just run size exclusion twice and skip the rest?',
    ez:'“Because of the load volume. It must be under five per cent of the column volume. So a litre of lysate would need a column the size of a room. And size exclusion separates only by size. So it cannot remove a contaminant of the same size. The yield is explicitly listed as low.”',
    ezcn:'因为<b>上样体积的限制</b>：<b>必须小于柱体积的 5%</b>——<b>一升裂解液就需要一根房间那么大的柱子</b>。<b>而且分子筛只按大小分离，所以去不掉一个刚好跟你的目标一样大的杂质</b>。<b>它的回收率在表上也明确写着「低」。</b>',
 en:'“Because of the load volume. Under 5 per cent of the column volume means you would need a column the size of a room to handle a litre of lysate. And size exclusion separates only by size, so it cannot remove a contaminant that happens to be the same size as your target. The yield is explicitly listed as low.”',
 cn:'⚠ 「a column the size of a room」<b>是个说法，不是一个算出来的数</b>；被追问就退回硬约束本身：5% 的上样上限加上一升裂解液，这两个数相乘就是结论。'},
{r:'中', q:'Your sample just came off an ammonium sulfate precipitation. What next?',
  ez:'“Hydrophobic interaction comes next. It can go straight on. No buffer exchange is needed. That sample is already at high salt. And hydrophobic interaction binds at high salt. Ion exchange would be different. There you would have to desalt first. Designing the order is largely one thing. You arrange each step to hand off cleanly to the next.”',
  ezcn:'<b>下一步是疏水相互作用层析，而且可以直接上样、不用换缓冲液</b>——<b>因为这个样品本来就在高盐里，而疏水层析正是在高盐下结合的。</b><b>如果下一步是离子交换就不行，得先脱盐。</b><b>排顺序这件事，很大程度上就是让每一步的产物能干净地交给下一步。</b>',
 en:'“Hydrophobic interaction, and it can go straight on with no buffer exchange, because that sample is already at high salt and hydrophobic interaction binds at high salt. If the next step were ion exchange you would have to desalt first. Designing the order is largely about arranging things so each step hands off cleanly to the next.”',
 cn:'<b>这一题是「缓冲液状态接力」那条约束的具体形式</b>，笔记标了 beyond the slides。答出来等于说明你知道顺序不只是「谁分辨率高」。<span class="pg">L4 s.16</span>'},
{r:'中', q:'Your target is in the flow-through. What went wrong?',
  ez:'“It did not bind. There are four usual causes. The column was overloaded past its capacity. The buffer conditions were wrong, so the protein did not carry the charge it needed. The tag was buried inside the folded protein. Then the resin could not reach it. Or the resin was damaged. Nickel is especially vulnerable to E D T A and to reducing agents.”',
  ezcn:'<b>它没结合上。</b><b>四个常见原因：上样超过了柱容量 · 缓冲条件不对，蛋白没带上它该带的电荷 · 标签被埋在折叠好的蛋白内部，填料够不着 · 或者填料坏了（镍柱对 EDTA 和还原剂特别脆弱）。</b>',
 en:'“It did not bind, and there are four usual causes. The column was overloaded past its capacity. The buffer conditions were wrong, so the protein did not carry the charge it needed. The tag was buried inside the folded protein where the resin could not reach it. Or the resin was damaged, and nickel is especially vulnerable to EDTA and to reducing agents.”',
 cn:'<b>先看 FT，是笔记给的诊断入口</b>（标了 beyond the slides）。它把失败分成两类：「没结合上」和「结合了但下不来」——<b>原因完全不同</b>。FT 干净但洗脱峰很小 ＝ 后一类，或者蛋白在柱上沉淀降解了。<span class="pg">L4 s.8–10</span>'},
{r:'中', q:'Why can a nickel column work in 6 M guanidinium when the others cannot?',
  ez:'“Because binding here is a coordination bond. It forms between histidine side chains and a metal ion. That does not require the protein to be folded. M B P and G S T and Strep are different. They depend on a native fold. Or they depend on protein recognition. A denaturant removes exactly that. So denaturing purification from inclusion bodies is committed. It essentially has to use a histidine tag.”',
  ezcn:'因为<b>这里的结合是组氨酸侧链跟金属离子之间的配位键，而那不要求蛋白是折叠的</b>。<b>MBP、GST、Strep 都不一样：它们依赖天然折叠或者蛋白识别，而变性剂拿掉的正好就是这个。</b><b>所以从包涵体做变性纯化，基本上就只能用组氨酸标签。</b>',
 en:'“Because binding is a coordination bond between the histidine side chains and a metal ion, and that does not require the protein to be folded. MBP, GST and Strep all depend on a native fold or on protein recognition, and a denaturant removes exactly that. So denaturing purification from inclusion bodies is essentially committed to a histidine tag.”',
 cn:'<b>这是 Ni-NTA 唯一真正独门的本事</b>，也是「选哪个标签」那三条规矩里的第一条。<span class="pg">L4 s.20</span> 变性剂把什么拆掉了，在卡 <b>01</b> 和卡 <b>x-bonds</b>。'}
]},

{g:'收尾 · 纯度和浓度', gn:'这两条是「纯化完了」这句话的证据。<b>公式题在这一组。</b>', items:[
{r:'高', q:'Why is it called SDS-PAGE and not just PAGE?',
    ez:'“Because S D S is doing three separate jobs. All of them are needed. It denatures the protein into a linear chain. It binds at roughly one molecule per two residues. So every protein ends with the same charge to mass ratio. And it makes everything rod shaped. In native P A G E it is different. Mobility depends on charge and size and shape together. So you cannot read a molecular weight from it.”',
    ezcn:'因为 <b>SDS 同时在干三件缺一不可的事</b>：<b>把蛋白变性成一条线性链</b>；<b>大约每两个残基结合一个 SDS 分子，于是所有蛋白的电荷/质量比都一样</b>；<b>而且把一切都变成棒状</b>。<b>天然 PAGE 里迁移率同时取决于电荷、大小和形状，所以从上面读不出分子量。</b>',
 en:'“Because SDS is doing three separate jobs and all of them are needed. It denatures the protein into a linear chain. It binds at roughly one molecule per two residues, so every protein ends with the same charge to mass ratio. And it makes everything rod-shaped. In native PAGE mobility depends on charge and size and shape together, so you cannot read a molecular weight from it.”',
 cn:'三件事<b>必须分开数出来</b>，这是这一节的核心（笔记标了 beyond the slides）。还原剂是<b>第四个、独立的</b>要素，不加就是非还原胶，用来看分子间二硫键。<span class="pg">L5 s.11</span>',
 good:'最干净的例子：<b>抗体</b>在还原胶上分成重链和轻链两条带，在非还原胶上是一条 150 kDa 的带。'},
{r:'高', q:'How do you determine the concentration?',
    ez:'“By absorbance at two hundred and eighty nanometres. Concentration equals absorbance over the extinction coefficient times the path length. A standard cuvette has a one centimetre path. No standard curve is needed here. The reason is that the extinction coefficient can be calculated. It is calculated from the sequence. Tryptophan absorbs most at that wavelength. Tyrosine comes next. Phenylalanine is far behind.”',
    ezcn:'<b>用 280 nm 的吸光度</b>：<b>浓度 ＝ 吸光度 ÷（消光系数 × 光程）</b>，<b>标准比色皿光程 1 cm</b>。⚠ <b>这里不需要标准曲线，理由是消光系数可以从序列算出来</b>。<b>280 nm 处吸得最多的是色氨酸，其次酪氨酸，苯丙氨酸远远落后。</b>',
 en:'“By absorbance at 280 nanometres. Concentration equals absorbance divided by the extinction coefficient times the path length, and a standard cuvette has a 1 centimetre path. The reason no standard curve is needed is that the extinction coefficient can be calculated from the sequence. Tryptophan absorbs most at 280, then tyrosine, with phenylalanine far behind.”',
 cn:'<b>=== 公式和推导（背之前先看懂这一段） ===</b><br><b>式子</b>：<code>A = ε · c · l</code><br>A 吸光度，无单位 · ε 摩尔消光系数 <code>M⁻¹cm⁻¹</code> · c 摩尔浓度 <code>M</code> · l 光程 <code>cm</code>。<br><br><b>四步</b>：<br>① 光走一小段 <code>dx</code>，被吸掉的<b>比例</b>正比于路上的分子数：<code>−dI/I = k·c·dx</code>。<b>按比例削减，不是按定量削减</b>，这是全式的起点。<br>② 积分：<code>ln(I₀/I) = k·c·l</code>。<b>对数就是从这一步来的。</b><br>③ 换底并把常数并进 ε：<code>A = log₁₀(I₀/I) = ε·c·l</code>。<br>④ 反解，<code>l = 1 cm</code> 时 <code>c = A₂₈₀/ε</code>；要 mg/mL 再乘分子量：<code>c(mg/mL) = A₂₈₀·M/ε</code>。<br><br><b>=== 一句话理解 ===</b><br><b>A280 是在数你自己的色氨酸，Bradford 是在数碱性和芳香族残基再跟 BSA 比。</b>一个的标尺长在你自己的序列上，另一个的标尺长在别人的蛋白上——这一句就解释了为什么前者不用曲线、后者必须做曲线而且换蛋白就可能不准。<br>⚠ <b>这套积分推导课上没给，是通用物理化学。</b>幻灯片给的是「消光系数可以从序列得到」和各方法的取舍。<span class="pg">L5 s.12–13</span>',
 warn:'⚠ 两处失效要能当场说：<b>核酸在 260–280 nm 也强吸收</b>，粗样品会被严重高估（查 A260/A280，纯蛋白约 <b>0.57</b>）；<b>不含色氨酸的蛋白</b>消光系数太低，测出来没有意义。'},
{r:'中', q:'When would you use Bradford instead?',
  ez:'“For crude lysate. Or for anything containing nucleic acid. The dye is not sensitive to nucleic acids. Absorbance at two eighty is. Bradford is sensitive down to one microgram. There are costs. It needs a calibration curve. The linear range is narrow. And different proteins respond very differently. The dye binds mainly basic and aromatic residues.”',
  ezcn:'<b>用在粗裂解液上，或者任何含核酸的样品上</b>——<b>因为这个染料对核酸不敏感，而 A280 敏感。</b><b>Bradford 能测到 1 µg。</b><b>代价是：需要做标准曲线、线性范围窄，而且不同蛋白的响应差别很大，因为染料主要结合碱性和芳香族残基。</b>',
 en:'“For crude lysate, or for anything containing nucleic acid, because the dye is not sensitive to nucleic acids the way absorbance at 280 is. It is sensitive down to 1 microgram. The cost is that it needs a calibration curve, the linear range is narrow, and different proteins respond very differently, because the dye binds mainly basic and aromatic residues.”',
 cn:'Bradford 的化学：酸性条件下的<b>考马斯亮蓝 G-250</b> 结合蛋白后，吸收峰从 <b>465 nm 移到 595 nm</b>。⚠ 去污剂（SDS、Triton）干扰严重。<b>有还原剂时不要用 BCA 或 Lowry</b>，铜化学会被破坏。<span class="pg">L5 s.12–13</span>'},
{r:'中', q:'What would you say the hardest part of a purification is?',
  ez:'“The hardest part is getting the first step right. Everything downstream inherits its buffer. It also inherits its volume. And I would avoid calling any of it simple. Each step leaves the sample in a particular condition. The next step has to accept that condition. So a choice made at capture constrains what is available later. It constrains what you can do at polishing.”',
  ezcn:'<b>最难的是把第一步做对</b>，<b>因为后面每一步都继承了它的缓冲液和它的体积。</b><b>而且我不会把其中任何一步说成「简单」：每一步都把样品留在某个特定的状态里，而下一步必须接受这个状态——所以在捕获那一步做的选择，限制了你在精纯那一步还剩下哪些选项。</b>',
 en:'“Getting the first step right, because everything downstream inherits its buffer and its volume. And I would avoid calling any of it simple. Each step leaves the sample in a particular condition, and the next step has to accept that condition, so a choice made at capture constrains what is available at polishing.”',
 cn:'⚠ <b>这一条是为一个说话习惯准备的。</b>2026-09-01 那场口试上，失分的三处之一是<b>用了一个撑不住的形容词（simple）</b>。形容词一出口，他就会问「哪里简单」，而那是一个没有好答案的问题。<b>把形容词换成一个机制</b>：不说 simple，说「下游继承上游的缓冲液和体积」。'}
]},
 {g:'怎么发现的', gn:'⚠ <b>2026-09-21 补的一组</b>（`tools/askgroups.py` 查出来这张卡缺它）。<b>这一科整科在捷克书之外，所以人名年份一律标 general。</b>⚠ <b>标了「待核」的年份别当确定的数报出去——说人名和实验就够。</b>', items:[
{r:'中', q:'How did chromatography begin, and what did each mode add?',
    ez:'“It began with plant pigments. Tswett poured an extract through a column of chalk. Coloured bands separated along the column. He named the method colour writing. That is what the word chromatography means. Every later mode kept the idea and changed the property. Gel filtration added separation by size. Porath and Flodin introduced it at the end of the fifties. Nothing binds in that mode. Ion exchange added separation by charge. Affinity chromatography added specific binding. Cuatrecasas and colleagues introduced that. So the history is one column and four different reasons to stick.”',
    ezcn:'<b>它从<b>植物色素</b>开始：Tswett 把提取液倒进一根装着碳酸钙的柱子，<b>有颜色的带沿着柱子分开了</b>；他把这个方法叫做「颜色书写」——<b>chromatography 这个词就是这么来的</b>。</b><b>后来的每一种模式都保留这个想法、换掉那个性质：<b>凝胶过滤</b>加进了「按大小分」（Porath 与 Flodin，五十年代末；<b>这一模式里什么都不结合</b>）· <b>离子交换</b>加进了「按电荷分」· <b>亲和层析</b>加进了「按特异结合分」（Cuatrecasas 等）。</b>⚠ <b>所以这段历史就是：<b>同一根柱子，四个不同的「为什么会黏住」</b>。</b>',
 en:'“It began with plant pigments. Tswett poured an extract through a column of chalk and coloured bands separated along the column. He named the method colour writing, and that is what the word chromatography means. Every later mode kept the idea and changed the property being exploited. Gel filtration added separation by size, introduced by Porath and Flodin at the end of the fifties, and nothing binds in that mode at all. Ion exchange added separation by charge. Affinity chromatography added specific binding, introduced by Cuatrecasas and colleagues. So the history is one column and four different reasons for something to stick to it.”',
 cn:'<b>通用知识，标 general。</b>Tswett 一般归到 1906 年；⚠ <b>其余年份待核</b>，说人名和「这一模式加进了什么」就够。<b>接口</b>：这一条正好是这张卡和 <b>pe-clone</b> 之间的那句话——<b>「模式之间变的只有：固定相被选来利用哪一种物理性质」</b>，历史和原理是同一句。'},
{r:'中', q:'Where did the histidine tag come from?',
    ez:'“It came from two things meeting. The first was immobilised metal affinity chromatography. Porath introduced it in the seventies. A metal ion is held on the resin. Histidine side chains coordinate that metal. So proteins rich in surface histidines are retained. The trouble is that few proteins are. The second thing was genetic engineering. You can add the histidines yourself. A short run of six is enough. Hochuli and colleagues put the two together. The tag went onto the gene rather than onto the protein. So the method stopped depending on what the protein happened to be. That is why one column now purifies almost anything.”',
    ezcn:'<b>它来自<b>两件事碰头</b>。</b><b>第一件是<b>固定化金属亲和层析（IMAC）</b>：Porath 七十年代提出——树脂上固定一个金属离子，<b>组氨酸侧链能配位这个金属</b>，所以表面富含组氨酸的蛋白会被留住。<b>麻烦在于这样的蛋白很少。</b></b><b>第二件是<b>基因工程</b>：既然天然的少，<b>那就自己加上去</b>——一小串六个就够。</b>⚠ <b>Hochuli 等人把两件事合在一起：<b>标签加在基因上，而不是加在蛋白上</b>，于是这个方法<b>不再取决于这个蛋白碰巧长什么样</b>——这就是为什么今天一根柱子几乎什么都能纯。</b>',
 en:'“It came from two things meeting. The first was immobilised metal affinity chromatography, introduced by Porath in the seventies. A metal ion is held on the resin and histidine side chains coordinate that metal, so proteins rich in surface histidines are retained. The trouble is that few proteins are. The second thing was genetic engineering, because the histidines can simply be added, and a short run of six is enough. Hochuli and colleagues put the two together. The tag goes onto the gene rather than onto the protein, so the method stopped depending on what the protein happened to be. That is why one column now purifies almost anything.”',
 cn:'<b>通用知识，标 general。</b>⚠ <b>年份待核</b>（IMAC 一般归七十年代中，His 标签一般归八十年代末）。<b>接口</b>：这一条是这张卡「捕获步用亲和」那一格的由来，也解释了 <b>pe-expr</b> 为什么把标签写进质粒元件清单里。'},
 ]}
]
});
